hadiths[451]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7297","Abū Dharr رضي الله عنه reported: A man called ʿAkkāf ibn Bishr al-Tamīmī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, ""O ʿAkkāf, do you have a wife?"" He said: No. He said, ""Not even a concubine?"" He said: No. He said, ""And are you well-off with good means?"" He said: I am well-off with good means. He said, ""Then you are one of the brothers of the devils. Had you been among the Christians you would have been one of their monks. Our Sunnah is marriage. The worst among you are your unmarried ones, and the most despised of your dead are your unmarried ones. Do you wrestle with the devils? The devils have no weapon more effective against the righteous than women, except those who are married; they are the purified ones, declared free of indecency. Woe to you, O ʿAkkāf, for women were the companions of Ayyūb and Dāwūd and Yūsuf and Kursuf."" Bishr ibn ʿAtiyyah said to him: Who is Kursuf, O Messenger of Allah? He said, ""A man who worshipped Allah on a seashore for three hundred years, fasting by day and standing in prayer by night, then he disbelieved in Allah the Almighty on account of a woman he fell in love with, and he abandoned the worship of Allah Almighty he had been upon. Then Allah Almighty reached him through some of his former good and accepted his repentance. Woe to you, O ʿAkkāf, marry, otherwise you are among the wavering."" He said: Marry me off, O Messenger of Allah. He said, ""I have married you to Karīmah bint Kulthūm al-Himyarī."" > **""Our Sunnah is marriage. The worst among you are your unmarried ones, and the most despised of your dead are your unmarried ones.""**"
"7298","ʿAtiyyah ibn Busr al-Māzinī رضي الله عنه reported: ʿAkkāf ibn Wadāʿah al-Hilālī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, ""O ʿAkkāf, do you have a wife?"" He said: No. He said, ""Not even a concubine?"" He said: No. He said, ""And are you healthy and well-off?"" He said: Yes, and praise be to Allah. He said, ""Then you are one of the brothers of the devils. Either you are among the monks of the Christians and thus one of them, or you are of us, so do as we do, for marriage is part of our Sunnah. The worst among you are your unmarried ones, and the most despised of your dead are your unmarried ones. Do they wrestle with the devils? They have no weapon against the righteous more effective than men and women, except those who are married; they are the purified ones, declared free of indecency."" Then he mentioned the hadith similar to the hadith of Abū Dharr, except that he said, ""Woe to you, O ʿAkkāf, marry, for you are among the wavering."" ʿAkkāf said: O Messenger of Allah, I shall not marry until you marry me to whomever you wish. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Then I have married you, in the name of Allah and His blessing, to Karīmah bint Kulthūm al-Himyarī."" > **""Do as we do, for marriage is part of our Sunnah. The worst among you are your unmarried ones, and the most despised of your dead are your unmarried ones.""**"
"7299","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: Had only a single day remained of my life, I would meet Allah with a wife. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ""The worst among you are your unmarried ones."" > **""The worst among you are your unmarried ones.""**"
"7300","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: Had I known that only ten nights remained of my life, I would have loved that a wife not be separated from me during them."
"7301","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed effeminate men who imitate women, and masculine women who imitate men, and celibate men who say, ""We shall not marry,"" and celibate women who say the same, and the lone rider in the desert. This weighed heavily upon the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until it became evident in their faces, and he said, ""The one who sleeps alone,"" meaning the one who travels alone through the desert at night. > **""The one who sleeps alone.""**"
"7302","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""Four Allah cursed above His Throne, and the angels said Amen over them: the one who fortifies himself against women and neither marries nor takes a concubine, lest a child be born to him; the man who imitates women though Allah created him male; the woman who imitates men though Allah created her female; and the one who misleads the poor."" Khālid ibn al-Zibriqān explained that this means mocking them, such as saying to the poor man, ""Come, let me give you something,"" and when the man comes to him he says, ""I have nothing with me""; or saying to the blind man, ""Beware of the well, beware of the beast,"" though there is nothing before him; or a man asking about the dwelling of a people and being directed to other than it. > **""Four Allah cursed above His Throne, and the angels said Amen over them.""**"
"7303","Abū Najīh reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever is well-off enough to marry and then does not marry is not of me."" > **""Whoever is well-off enough to marry and then does not marry is not of me.""**"
"7304","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to some young men of Quraysh and said: ""O assembly of youths, whoever among you has the means, let him marry, and otherwise fasting is upon him, for it is a restraint for him."" > **""O assembly of youths, whoever among you has the means, let him marry, and otherwise fasting is upon him, for it is a restraint for him.""**"
"7305","ʿUbayd ibn Saʿd conveyed from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""Whoever loves my nature, let him follow my Sunnah, and marriage is part of my Sunnah."" > **""Whoever loves my nature, let him follow my Sunnah, and marriage is part of my Sunnah.""**"
"7306","Anas رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""O assembly of youths, whoever among you has means, let him marry, and whoever does not, fasting is upon him."" The narrator thought he added, ""For it is a restraint for him."" > **""O assembly of youths, whoever among you has means, let him marry, and whoever does not, fasting is upon him.""**"
"7307","Anas رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command marriage and would forbid celibacy with severe prohibition, and he would say, ""Marry the loving and fertile, for I shall boast of your numbers before the Prophets on the Day of Resurrection."" > **""Marry the loving and fertile, for I shall boast of your numbers before the Prophets on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"7308","Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀs رضي الله عنه reported that ʿUthmān ibn Mazʿūn رضي الله عنه said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to be castrated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, ""Allah has replaced monasticism for us with the tolerant straight religion and the proclamation of Allah is Most Great upon every elevation. If you are of us, then do as we do."" > **""Allah has replaced monasticism for us with the tolerant straight religion and the proclamation of Allah is Most Great upon every elevation. If you are of us, then do as we do.""**"
"7309","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Whoever marries has been given half of worship."" > **""Whoever marries has been given half of worship.""**"
"7310","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Whoever marries has completed half of faith, so let him fear Allah in the remaining half."" > **""Whoever marries has completed half of faith, so let him fear Allah in the remaining half.""**"
"7311","Abū Najīh reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Poor, poor, poor is a man who has no wife, even if he has abundant wealth. Poor, poor, poor is a woman who has no husband, even if she has abundant wealth."" > **""Poor, poor, poor is a man who has no wife, even if he has abundant wealth. Poor, poor, poor is a woman who has no husband, even if she has abundant wealth.""**"
"7312","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""O youths of Quraysh, do not commit adultery. Guard your private parts. Know that whoever guards his private part shall have Paradise."" > **""O youths of Quraysh, do not commit adultery. Guard your private parts. Know that whoever guards his private part shall have Paradise.""**"
"7313","In a narration: ""Know that whoever guards his private part shall enter Paradise."" > **""Know that whoever guards his private part shall enter Paradise.""**"
"7314","Sahl ibn Hunayf رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Marry, for I shall boast of your numbers before the nations."" > **""Marry, for I shall boast of your numbers before the nations.""**"
"7315","Abū Talhah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""O youths of Quraysh, do not commit adultery. Whoever keeps his youth sound shall have Paradise."" > **""O youths of Quraysh, do not commit adultery. Whoever keeps his youth sound shall have Paradise.""**"
"7316","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Any youth who marries in his early years, his devil cries out: Woe to him, woe to him, he has protected his religion from me."" > **""Any youth who marries in his early years, his devil cries out: Woe to him, woe to him, he has protected his religion from me.""**"
"7317","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""We have taken of your world nothing but your women."" > **""We have taken of your world nothing but your women.""**"
"7318","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Five are of the practices of the Messengers: modesty, forbearance, cupping, perfume, and marriage."" > **""Five are of the practices of the Messengers: modesty, forbearance, cupping, perfume, and marriage.""**"
"7319","Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh رضي الله عنهما reported: A youth came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to be castrated. He said, ""Fast, and ask Allah of His bounty."" > **""Fast, and ask Allah of His bounty.""**"
"7320","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to be castrated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""The castration of my nation is fasting and standing in prayer."" > **""The castration of my nation is fasting and standing in prayer.""**"
"7321","ʿUthmān ibn Mazʿūn رضي الله عنه said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man for whom remaining unmarried during military expeditions is hard, so will you permit me to be castrated? He said, ""No. Rather, fasting is upon you, O Ibn Mazʿūn, for it curbs desire."" > **""No. Rather, fasting is upon you, O Ibn Mazʿūn, for it curbs desire.""**"
"7322","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: A man complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of being unmarried and said: Shall I not be castrated? The Prophet ﷺ said to him, ""He is not of us who castrates or seeks castration. Rather fast, and leave the hair of your body."" > **""He is not of us who castrates or seeks castration. Rather fast, and leave the hair of your body.""**"
"7323","Samurah رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid a man from remaining celibate and from deeming it unlawful to enter the houses of the believers."
"7324","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, ""Whoever marries a woman for her honor, Allah will increase him only in disgrace. Whoever marries her for her wealth, Allah will increase him only in poverty. Whoever marries her for her beauty, Allah will increase him only in lowliness. And whoever marries a woman marrying her only to lower his gaze, or to guard his private part, or to uphold kinship, Allah will bless him through her and bless her through him."" > **""Whoever marries a woman for her honor, Allah will increase him only in disgrace. Whoever marries her for her wealth, Allah will increase him only in poverty. Whoever marries her for her beauty, Allah will increase him only in lowliness. And whoever marries a woman marrying her only to lower his gaze, or to guard his private part, or to uphold kinship, Allah will bless him through her and bless her through him.""**"
"7325","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported: I married a woman in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, ""O Jābir, have you married?"" I said: Yes. He said, ""A virgin or a previously married woman?"" I said: A previously married woman. He said, ""Why not a virgin, whom you would play with and who would play with you?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have sisters, and I feared she would come between me and them. He said, ""A woman is married for her religion, her wealth, and her beauty, so hold to the one with religion, may your hands be dusty."" > **""A woman is married for her religion, her wealth, and her beauty, so hold to the one with religion, may your hands be dusty.""**"
"7326","Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""A woman is married for one of these qualities: her beauty, her wealth, her character, and her religion. So hold to the one with religion and character, may your right hand be dusty."" > **""A woman is married for one of these qualities: her beauty, her wealth, her character, and her religion. So hold to the one with religion and character, may your right hand be dusty.""**"
"7327","ʿAwf ibn Mālik al-Ashjaʿī رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Visit the sick and follow the funeral procession. There is no harm upon you if you do not attend the wedding feast. There is no harm upon you if you do not marry a woman for her beauty, for perhaps she brings no good. There is no harm upon you if you do not marry a woman for her abundant wealth, for perhaps her wealth brings no good. Rather seek those with religion and trustworthiness."" > **""Visit the sick and follow the funeral procession. There is no harm upon you if you do not attend the wedding feast. There is no harm upon you if you do not marry a woman for her beauty, for perhaps she brings no good. There is no harm upon you if you do not marry a woman for her abundant wealth, for perhaps her wealth brings no good. Rather seek those with religion and trustworthiness.""**"
"7328","ʿAlī رضي الله عنه reported that he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said, ""What is best for a woman?"" They fell silent. When I returned I said to Fātimah رضي الله عنها: What is best for women? She said: That men do not see them. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, ""She is Fātimah, a part of me."" > **""She is Fātimah, a part of me.""**"
"7329","Umm Mubashshir رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ proposed to the widow of al-Barāʾ ibn Maʿrūr. She said: I had stipulated to my husband that I would not marry after him. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""That is not proper."" > **""That is not proper.""**"
"7330","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Marry women, for they will bring you wealth."" > **""Marry women, for they will bring you wealth.""**"
"7331","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Part of the blessing of a woman is the ease of her proposal, the ease of her dowry, and the ease of her womb,"" meaning her fitness to bear children. > **""Part of the blessing of a woman is the ease of her proposal, the ease of her dowry, and the ease of her womb.""**"
"7332","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The greatest of women in blessing are the easiest of them in provision,"" meaning in dowry and upkeep. > **""The greatest of women in blessing are the easiest of them in provision.""**"
"7333","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have married off my daughter, and I would love for you to help me with something. He said, ""I have nothing with me now, but tomorrow bring me a wide-mouthed flask and a stick of wood."" The hadith continues among the rare reports. > **""I have nothing with me now, but tomorrow bring me a wide-mouthed flask and a stick of wood.""**"
"7334","Rabīʿah al-Aslamī رضي الله عنه reported: I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me, ""O Rabīʿah, will you not marry?"" I said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not wish to marry, and I have nothing with which to maintain a wife, and I do not wish anything to distract me from you. He turned away from me, and I served him as I served him. Then he said to me a second time, ""O Rabīʿah, will you not marry?"" I said: I do not wish to marry; I have nothing with which to maintain a wife, and I do not wish anything to distract me from you. He turned away from me. Then I returned to myself and said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ knows better than I what benefits me in this world and the Hereafter. By Allah, if he says to me, ""Will you marry,"" I shall surely say, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah, command me as you wish."" Then he said to me, ""O Rabīʿah, will you not marry?"" I said: Yes indeed, command me as you wish. He said, ""Go to the household of so-and-so,"" a clan of the Ansār among whom there had been some distance from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ""and say to them: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to you, commanding you to marry me to so-and-so,"" naming a woman among them. So I went to them and said to them: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to you, commanding you to marry me to so-and-so. They said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shall not return except with his need fulfilled. So they married me to her, treated me kindly, and did not ask me for proof, though I had no dowry with me. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""O Buraydah al-Aslamī, gather for him the weight of a date-pit in gold."" So they gathered for me the weight of a date-pit in gold. I took what they had gathered for me and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, ""Take this to them and say to them: This is her dowry."" So I went to them and said: This is her dowry. They accepted it, were pleased with it, and said: Much and good. Then I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ grieving, and he said, ""O Rabīʿah, why are you grieving?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have never seen people more generous than them. They were pleased with what I brought them, treated me well, and said, ""Much and good,"" yet I have nothing with which to hold a wedding feast. He said, ""O Buraydah, gather for him a sheep."" So they gathered for me a great fat ram. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, ""Go to ʿĀʾishah and tell her to send the basket in which there is food."" So I went to her and told her what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had commanded me, and she said: This is the basket; in it are seven measures of barley. By Allah, we have no food besides it this morning. Take it. So I took it and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of what ʿĀʾishah had said. He said, ""Take this to them and say to them: Let this become bread with you by morning, and this meat stew."" They said: As for the bread, we shall suffice you of it, but as for the ram, you suffice us of it. So I and some men of Aslam took the ram, slaughtered it, skinned it, and cooked it, and by morning we had bread and meat. I held a wedding feast and invited the Prophet ﷺ. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ later gave me land and gave Abū Bakr land, and worldly means came to us. We differed over a cluster of dates on a palm tree. I said: It is within my boundary. Abū Bakr said: It is within my boundary. There were words between me and Abū Bakr, and Abū Bakr said to me a word I disliked, and he regretted it. He said to me: O Rabīʿah, say back to me the like of it, so that there may be retaliation. I said: I shall not do it. Abū Bakr said: You shall surely say it, or I shall complain of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: I shall not do it. He left the land and Abū Bakr set out to the Prophet ﷺ, and I set out following him. Some men of Aslam came and said to me: May Allah have mercy on Abū Bakr, for what does he seek the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against, when he is the one who said to you what he said? I said: Do you know who this is? This is Abū Bakr al-Siddīq. This is the second of two. This is the elder of the Muslims. Beware, lest he turn and see you aiding me against him, and he becomes angry, and comes to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who becomes angry for his anger, and Allah Almighty becomes angry for the anger of them both, and Rabīʿah perishes. He said: What do you command us? He said: Go back. So Abū Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, set out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I followed him alone until he came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he narrated the account as it had been. He raised his head to me and said to me, ""O Rabīʿah, what is between you and al-Siddīq?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, it was such-and-such. He said to me a word I disliked. He said to me: Say as I said, so that there may be retaliation, but I refused. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Yes, do not answer him back. Rather say: May Allah forgive you, O Abū Bakr."" So I said: May Allah forgive you, O Abū Bakr. Al-Hasan said: Then Abū Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, turned away weeping. > **""O Rabīʿah, will you not marry? Do not answer him back. Rather say: May Allah forgive you, O Abū Bakr.""**"
"7335","Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Three acts, whoever performs them trusting in Allah and seeking reward, it is binding upon Allah to aid him and bless him: whoever strives to free a slave trusting in Allah and seeking reward, it is binding upon Allah to aid him and bless him. Whoever marries trusting in Allah and seeking reward, it is binding upon Allah to aid him and bless him. And whoever revives dead land trusting in Allah and seeking reward, it is binding upon Allah to aid him and bless him."" > **""Three acts, whoever performs them trusting in Allah and seeking reward, it is binding upon Allah to aid him and bless him.""**"
"7336","Maʿqil ibn Yasār رضي الله عنه reported: Nothing was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than horses. Then he said: O Allah, pardon; except women are different."
"7337","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""We have taken of your world nothing but your women."" > **""We have taken of your world nothing but your women.""**"
"7338","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Marry the mothers of children, for I shall boast of them before the nations on the Day of Resurrection."" > **""Marry the mothers of children, for I shall boast of them before the nations on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"7339","Anas رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command marriage and would forbid celibacy with severe prohibition, and he would say, ""Marry the loving and fertile, for I shall boast of your numbers before the Prophets on the Day of Resurrection."" > **""Marry the loving and fertile, for I shall boast of your numbers before the Prophets on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"7340","ʿIyād ibn Ghanm رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, ""O ʿIyād, do not marry an old woman nor a barren one, for I shall boast of your numbers before the nations."" > **""O ʿIyād, do not marry an old woman nor a barren one, for I shall boast of your numbers before the nations.""**"
"7341","Muʿāwiyah ibn Haydah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""A dark fertile woman is better than a beautiful one who does not bear children. I shall boast of your numbers before the nations on the Day of Resurrection, until the miscarried child shall be brought, held back at the gate of Paradise. It shall be said to him: Enter Paradise. He shall say: O my Lord, and my parents? It shall be said to him: Enter Paradise, you and your parents."" > **""A dark fertile woman is better than a beautiful one who does not bear children. I shall boast of your numbers before the nations on the Day of Resurrection, until the miscarried child shall be brought, held back at the gate of Paradise. It shall be said to him: Enter Paradise. He shall say: O my Lord, and my parents? It shall be said to him: Enter Paradise, you and your parents.""**"
"7342","Hafsah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""None of you should abandon seeking children, for when a man dies and has no child, his name is cut off."" > **""None of you should abandon seeking children, for when a man dies and has no child, his name is cut off.""**"
"7343","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""For one of you to raise a puppy after fifty-four years is better for him than to raise a child of his own loins."" > **""For one of you to raise a puppy after fifty-four years is better for him than to raise a child of his own loins.""**"
"7344","Abū al-Dardāʾ رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Hold to concubines, for they are blessed in womb."" > **""Hold to concubines, for they are blessed in womb.""**"
"7345","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Hold to virgins, for they are most fruitful in womb, sweetest in mouth, least in scheming, and most content with little."" > **""Hold to virgins, for they are most fruitful in womb, sweetest in mouth, least in scheming, and most content with little.""**"
"7346","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Marry virgins, for they are sweetest in mouth, most fruitful in womb, and most content with little."" > **""Marry virgins, for they are sweetest in mouth, most fruitful in womb, and most content with little.""**"
"7347","Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah رضي الله عنه reported: We were with the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, ""O so-and-so, have you married?"" He said: No. He said to me, ""Have you married?"" I said: Yes. He said, ""A virgin or a previously married woman?"" I said: No, rather a previously married woman. He said, ""Why not a virgin, whom you bite and who bites you?"" > **""Why not a virgin, whom you bite and who bites you?""**"
"7348","Sahlah bint ʿĀsim ibn ʿAdī رضي الله عنها reported: I was born on the day of Hunayn, the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Hunayn. He named me Sahlah and said, ""May Allah ease your affair."" He allotted me a share and married me to ʿAbd al-Rahmān ibn ʿAwf on the day I was born. > **""May Allah ease your affair.""**"
"7349","Kardam ibn Sufyān al-Thaqafī رضي الله عنه reported that a man said: O Messenger of Allah. He bent toward him and the man said: Which army was at ʿIthrān? The Prophet ﷺ recognized that army. Tāriq ibn al-Muraqqaʿ said: Who will give me a spear for its reward? I said: What is its reward? He said: The first daughter born to me, I shall marry her to him. So I gave him my spear, then I forgot of him for years. Then it reached me that a daughter had been born to him and she had grown up. I said: Send my wife to me. He said: Not without a dowry. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Do you know which woman she is?"" I said: She has seen poverty and white hair, meaning she is grown. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""It is better for you neither to sin nor to cause sin. Leave her alone."" > **""It is better for you neither to sin nor to cause sin. Leave her alone.""**"
"7350","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: The example of one who frees his concubine then marries her is like the example of one who donates a sacrificial camel then rides it."
"7351","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Four are given their reward twice: the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, whoever of the People of the Book accepts Islam, a man who had a slave girl who pleased him, so he freed her then married her, and an owned slave who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters."" > **""Four are given their reward twice: the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, whoever of the People of the Book accepts Islam, a man who had a slave girl who pleased him, so he freed her then married her, and an owned slave who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters.""**"
"7352","Al-Mustawrid ibn al-Ahnaf reported: A man came to Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه and said: My uncle married me to his slave girl, and she bore me children, and now he wishes to enslave them. He said: That is not his right. > **""That is not his right.""**"
"7353","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""The Hour shall not come until you return to warring, and until a man shall turn to a Nabataean woman and marry her for livelihood, leaving the daughter of his paternal uncle without looking at her."" > **""The Hour shall not come until you return to warring, and until a man shall turn to a Nabataean woman and marry her for livelihood, leaving the daughter of his paternal uncle without looking at her.""**"
"7354","Talhah رضي الله عنه reported: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, ""One who marries among his people is like one who plants greenery in his own house."" > **""One who marries among his people is like one who plants greenery in his own house.""**"
"7355","Sahlah bint Suhayl رضي الله عنها reported that she said: O Messenger of Allah, Sālim, the freed slave of Abū Hudhayfah, enters upon me, and he is bearded. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Nurse him."" She said: How can I nurse him when he is bearded? So she nursed him, and he would then enter upon her. > **""Nurse him.""**"
"7356","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Fosterage prohibits what lineage prohibits, of maternal uncle, paternal uncle, or nephew."" > **""Fosterage prohibits what lineage prohibits, of maternal uncle, paternal uncle, or nephew.""**"
"7357","Thawbān رضي الله عنه reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: ""Fosterage prohibits what lineage prohibits."" > **""Fosterage prohibits what lineage prohibits.""**"
"7358","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""What is prohibited by lineage is prohibited by fosterage."" > **""What is prohibited by lineage is prohibited by fosterage.""**"
"7359","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""What is prohibited by lineage is prohibited by foster suckling."" > **""What is prohibited by lineage is prohibited by foster suckling.""**"
"7360","Abū Jaʿfar reported: It was said to Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah رضي الله عنه: Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I heard him say, ""The foster brother's daughter and the foster sister's daughter are not lawful,"" meaning in marriage. > **""The foster brother's daughter and the foster sister's daughter are not lawful.""**"
"7361","Al-Nakhaʿī reported that ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنهم said: Fosterage prohibits, little of it and much of it."
"7362","ʿAmr ibn Dīnār reported: A man came to Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما and said: Ibn al-Zubayr claims that one or two sucks in fosterage do not prohibit. Ibn ʿUmar said: The judgment of Allah and His Messenger is better than the judgment of Ibn al-Zubayr. Little fosterage and much of it are alike. > **""The judgment of Allah and His Messenger is better than the judgment of Ibn al-Zubayr. Little fosterage and much of it are alike.""**"
"7363","Al-Zubayr رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""One suck and two sucks, and one mouthful and two mouthfuls, do not prohibit."" > **""One suck and two sucks, and one mouthful and two mouthfuls, do not prohibit.""**"
"7364","Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The ʿanqah does not prohibit."" We said: What is the ʿanqah? He said, ""A woman gives birth, milk comes in her breast, and she nurses her neighbor's girl once or twice."" > **""The ʿanqah does not prohibit.""**"
"7365","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""One suck and two sucks of fosterage do not prohibit, and nothing of it prohibits except what opens the intestines."" > **""One suck and two sucks of fosterage do not prohibit, and nothing of it prohibits except what opens the intestines.""**"
"7366","Hafsah رضي الله عنها reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not deem fosterage prohibiting except ten nursings or more than ten."
"7367","ʿAlī ibn Abī Tālib رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""There is no fosterage after weaning, no orphanhood after puberty, no silence of a day until night, and no divorce except after marriage."" > **""There is no fosterage after weaning, no orphanhood after puberty, no silence of a day until night, and no divorce except after marriage.""**"
"7368","Abū ʿAtiyyah reported that a man came to Abū Mūsā رضي الله عنه and said: A woman's breast swelled, so he, meaning her husband, began to suck it and spit it out, and some entered his belly. He said: I do not see her lawful for him. Then he came to Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه and asked him about that. He said: She has not become unlawful to you. Only that fosterage prohibits which grows flesh and strengthens bone, and there is no fosterage after weaning. It was conveyed to Abū Mūsā, and he said: Do not ask me about anything so long as this one remains among us from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. > **""Only that fosterage prohibits which grows flesh and strengthens bone, and there is no fosterage after weaning.""**"
"7369","Abū Quʿays رضي الله عنه came to ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها and sought permission to enter upon her, and she disliked granting him permission. When the Prophet ﷺ came, she said: O Messenger of Allah, Abū Quʿays came to me and I refused to permit him. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Let him enter upon you, for he is your paternal uncle."" Abū Quʿays was the brother of the wet nurse of ʿĀʾishah. > **""Let him enter upon you, for he is your paternal uncle.""**"
"7370","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ: What removes from me the blame of fosterage, meaning the due right attached to it? He said, ""A fine slave or maidservant."" > **""A fine slave or maidservant.""**"
"7371","ʿUbādah, meaning Ibn al-Sāmit رضي الله عنه, reported that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said, ""The giving of a fine slave or maidservant."" > **""The giving of a fine slave or maidservant.""**"
"7372","On the authority of Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — Yunus ibn Habib explained that al-warha' means the foolish woman: > **""Do not seek suckling from the foolish woman.""**"
"7373","On the authority of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade seeking suckling from the foolish woman."
"7374","On the authority of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""A woman is not taken in marriage upon her paternal aunt, nor upon her maternal aunt.""**"
"7375","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""A woman is not taken in marriage upon her paternal aunt, nor upon her maternal aunt.""**"
"7376","On his authority — Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them) — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaned against a House and exhorted the people and reminded them, saying: > **""Let no one pray after Asr until the night, nor after Fajr until the sun rises; let no woman travel a distance of three days except with a mahram relative; and let no woman be contracted in marriage upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt.""**"
"7377","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him), in a report raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): > **""A woman is not taken in marriage upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt, and let not a woman ask for the divorce of her sister so as to overturn what is in her dish for herself.""**"
"7378","On the authority of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married upon her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt; and he forbade two kinds of dress — al-samma', and that a man sit with his knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part; and he forbade fasting the Day of Adha and the Day of Fitr, and prayer after Fajr until the sun rises and after Asr until the sun sets."
"7379","On the authority of Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married upon her paternal aunt or upon her maternal aunt."
"7380","On the authority of Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married upon her paternal aunt or upon her maternal aunt."
"7381","On the authority of Attab ibn Aseed (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: > **""A woman is not taken in marriage upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt.""**"
"7382","On the authority of Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""A woman and her paternal aunt are not brought together, nor a woman and her maternal aunt.""**"
"7383","On the authority of Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to contract temporary marriage for a garment."
"7384","On the authority of Sabrah al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Year of the Conquest, and we stayed fifteen to thirty days and nights. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us permission for mutah. I went out with a cousin of mine in the lower part of Makkah — or he said, in the upper part of Makkah — and we met a young woman as if from Banu Amir ibn Sasah, tall-necked like a young she-camel. I was rather unsightly, wearing a new fine cloak, while my cousin wore a worn-out cloak. We said to her: > **""Would one of us have temporary marriage with you?""** She said: > **""Is that lawful?""** We said: > **""Yes.""** She began looking at my cousin, so I said to her: > **""This cloak of mine is new and fine, while my cousin's cloak is worn and threadbare.""** She said: > **""There is no harm in this cloak of your cousin.""** So he contracted temporary marriage with her, and we had not yet left Makkah when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"7385","On the authority of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the expedition of Tabuk and alighted at Thaniyyat al-Wada. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw lamps and saw women weeping, so he asked: > **""What is this?""** It was said: They are women weeping, with whom mutah had been contracted. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""It has been made forbidden — marriage, divorce, the waiting period, and inheritance have demolished mutah.""**"
"7386","On the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: We went out with the women with whom we had contracted mutah until we came to Thaniyyat al-Rikab, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, these are the women with whom we contracted mutah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""They are forbidden until the Day of Resurrection.""** Then they bade us farewell there, and for that reason it was named Thaniyyat al-Wada, whereas before that it was only Thaniyyat al-Rikab."
"7387","On the authority of Thalabah ibn al-Hakam (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutah on the Day of Khaybar."
"7388","Salim ibn Abdullah said: Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) was approached and it was said to him: Ibn Abbas commands temporary marriage. Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said: Glory be to Allah, I do not think Ibn Abbas would do this. They said: Indeed he commands it. He said: Was Ibn Abbas anything but a small boy when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us? Then Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it to us, and we were not fornicators."
"7389","On the authority of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that he was asked about mutah and said: It is unlawful. It was said: Ibn Abbas sees no harm in it. He said: By Allah, Ibn Abbas well knows that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it on the Day of Khaybar, and we were not fornicators."
"7390","On the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him): It was only for one who could not find means, then when the rulings of marriage, divorce, waiting period, and inheritance were revealed, it was forbidden."
"7391","Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah said: Ali and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) spoke about mutah with women, and Ali said to him: You are a bewildered man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutah with women at the Farewell Hajj."
"7392","Saeed ibn Jubayr said: I said to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): Do you know what you have done and what you have given fatwa about? Riders have carried your fatwa and poets have spoken of it. He asked: What did they say? I said: They said — He said to the old man when his sitting grew long: O companion, have you any desire for the fatwa of Ibn Abbas? Have you any desire for a lenient companion, a loving girl who would be your abode until the people depart? So he said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. By Allah, I did not give fatwa to this effect, nor did I intend this, and I permitted nothing of it except what Allah permitted of carrion, blood, and the flesh of swine — that is, only under dire necessity."
"7393","On the authority of Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I and a companion of mine were haggling with a woman over the term, and she was haggling with us, when a caller came to us and informed us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had forbidden temporary marriage, and had forbidden eating every fanged beast of prey and domestic donkeys."
"7394","On the authority of al-Harith ibn Ghaziyyah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of the Conquest of Makkah saying three times: > **""Temporary marriage with women is unlawful.""**"
"7395","On the authority of Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only permitted mutah for us because of a severe need that afflicted the people, then he forbade it afterwards."
"7396","On the authority of Kab ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage with women."
"7397","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed: > **""There is no shighar in Islam.""**"
"7398","On the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid shighar between women."
"7399","On the authority of Wail ibn Hujr (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"7400","On the authority of Ubayy ibn Kab (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""There is no shighar in Islam.""** They asked: What is shighar? He said: > **""Marrying a woman in exchange for a woman, with no dowry between them.""**"
"7401","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: > **""He is not of us who plunders.""** And he said: > **""There is no shighar in Islam — and shighar is that two women be married, one in exchange for the other, without dowry.""**"
"7402","On the authority of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the muhallil and the one for whom tahleel is done."
"7403","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), in a similar report with the addition: She then came to him afterwards and informed him that he had touched her — that is, consummated with her — yet he forbade her to return to her first husband and said: > **""O Allah, if his believing in it is in order to make her lawful for Rifaa, then do not complete another marriage for him.""** She then came to Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) during their caliphates, and both of them likewise forbade her."
"7404","Nafi, the freedman of Ibn Umar, reported that a man asked Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): My maternal uncle parted from his wife and was seized by grief and distress over it, so I wished to marry her without his commanding me or knowing of it — meaning to divorce her and make her lawful for him. Ibn Umar said: No, except a marriage of genuine desire — if she suits you, keep her, and if you dislike her, part from her. Otherwise, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to count this as fornication."
"7405","On the authority of Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram, and was cupped while in ihram."
"7406","Through her — Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) — that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while in ihram."
"7407","On the authority of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while in ihram."
"7408","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while both of them were in ihram."
"7409","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while he was out of ihram."
"7410","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), concerning His saying, Exalted is He: There is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord [2:198] — that is, there is no harm upon you in buying and selling before ihram and after it. As for ihram, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that one marry, or give in marriage, or slaughter, until he completes his ihram."
"7411","Ikrimah ibn Khalid said: I asked Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) about a woman a man wished to marry while he was outside Makkah and intended Umrah or Hajj. He said: Do not marry her while you are in ihram; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that."
"7412","On the authority of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The one in ihram does not marry, nor propose, nor is a proposal made on his behalf.""**"
"7413","On the authority of Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The one in ihram does not marry, nor is he given in marriage, nor does he propose, nor is a proposal made on his behalf.""**"
"7414","Maymun ibn Mihran said: I came to Safiyyah bint Shaybah when she was an elderly woman and asked her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marry Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while in ihram? She said: No; he married her while both of them were out of ihram."
"7415","On the authority of Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who pursues a woman unlawfully — may he then marry her mother? — or pursues the mother unlawfully — may he then marry her daughter? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The unlawful does not forbid the lawful; only what is through a lawful marriage forbids.""**"
"7416","Ibn Masud and Aishah (may Allah be pleased with them) said: Concerning a man who commits fornication with a woman and then marries her — the two remain fornicators as long as they stay together."
"7417","Ibn Sirin said: Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a man who commits fornication with a woman and then marries her. He said: They are both fornicators as long as they stay together. It was said to Ibn Masud: What if they repent and amend? He recited — And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds and knows what you do [42:25] — and Ibn Masud kept repeating it until we thought he saw no harm in it after true repentance and amendment."
"7418","Abu Salih said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Ask me, for you will never ask the like of me. So Ibn al-Kawwa said: Tell us about two owned sisters and about the foster brother's daughter. He said: Ask about what concerns you, for you are going into bewilderment. He said: I only ask about what we do not know; as for what we know, we do not ask about it. He said: As for the two owned sisters, one verse permitted them and another verse forbade them — I neither command it, nor forbid it, nor would I do it, nor would my household."
"7419","Qatadah said: A man argued with Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) about combining two sisters, saying: Allah has permitted for me what my right hand possesses. He replied: Your camel is also of what your right hand possesses."
"7420","Qatadah reported that Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forbade twelve women, and I dislike twelve further cases — a slave girl and her mother together, two sisters brought together, a slave girl whom your father has had, a slave girl whom your son has had, a slave girl who has committed fornication, a slave girl observing the waiting period of another, a slave girl who has a husband, your slave girl who is a polytheist, and your foster paternal and maternal aunts."
"7421","On the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: > **""Allah has permitted three ways with women: marriage with inheritance, marriage without inheritance, and possession of the right hand.""**"
"7422","Abu Amr al-Shaybani said: A man asked Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) about one who divorces his wife before consummating with her — may he marry her daughter? He said: Yes. So he married her and she bore him a child. He then came to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him. He said: Separate them. He said: She has borne a child. He said: Even if she bore him ten, separate them."
"7423","In another narration: Abdullah — Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) — gave concession in sarf, and in the case of a man who married a woman who then died before he consummated with her, that he may marry her mother."
"7424","Atiyyah ibn Qays al-Kalai said: Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with them) proposed to Umm al-Darda after the death of Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with them). Umm al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I heard Abu al-Darda say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: > **""Any woman whose husband dies and who then marries after him belongs to the last of her husbands.""** And I would never prefer anyone over Abu al-Darda. So Muawiyah wrote to her: Then fasting is upon you, for it curbs desire."
"7425","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to a woman of his people called Sawdah, who had lost her husband to death and had five or six children. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: > **""What prevents you from me?""** She said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, nothing prevents me from you in that you are not the most beloved of creation to me, but I would honour you from these children clamouring at your head morning and evening. He said: > **""Has anything besides that prevented you from me?""** She said: No, by Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""May Allah have mercy on you. The best women who ride the rumps of camels are the righteous women of Quraysh — most tender to a child in his infancy and most caring for a husband in his means.""**"
"7426","On the authority of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: > **""The best women who ride camels are the women of Quraysh — most tender to a child in his infancy and most compassionate to a husband despite his meagre means.""** Then Abu Hurairah said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) well knew that the daughter of Imran never rode a camel."
"7427","On the authority of Talhah ibn Ubaydullah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the road to Makkah: > **""The best women who ride camels are the women of Quraysh — most tender to a child and most caring for a husband.""**"
"7428","On the authority of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to me, and I said: I have no aversion to you, O Messenger of Allah, but I do not wish to marry while my children are small. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Why not? The best women who ride camels are the women of Quraysh — most tender to a child in his infancy and most caring for a husband in his means.""**"
"7429","Zayd ibn Abi al-Attab said: Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) stood upon the minbar and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: > **""The best women who ride camels are the women of Quraysh — most caring for a husband in his means and most tender to a child in his infancy.""**"
"7430","Aslam, the freedman of Umar, said: Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) summoned Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) and spoke to him privately. Then Ali rose and came to the Suffah, where he found al-Abbas, Aqeel, and al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them), and consulted them about marrying Umm Kulthum to Umar. Aqeel became angry and said: O Ali, days, months, and years only increase you in blindness in your affair; by Allah, if you do it, such-and-such will happen — listing things — and went off dragging his garment. Ali said to al-Abbas: By Allah, that is not counsel from him; rather the stick of Umar has driven him to what you see. By Allah, it is not aversion to you, O Aqeel, but Umar ibn al-Khattab told me: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: > **""Every tie and lineage is cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage.""** So Umar laughed and said: Woe to Aqeel, a witless fool."
"7431","Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) proposed Umm Kulthum to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: She is too young for that. Ali then said to al-Hasan and al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them): Marry your uncle. They said: She is a woman like other women; she may choose for herself. So Ali rose in anger, and al-Hasan held his garment and said: O father, we cannot bear your estrangement."
"7432","On the authority of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Three are of the happiness of the son of Adam, and three are of his misery. Of his happiness: a righteous wife, a good dwelling, and a good mount. And of his misery: an evil wife, a bad dwelling, and a bad mount.""**"
"7433","On the authority of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: > **""Three break the back: an evil spouse — her husband trusts her while she betrays him; a ruler who angers Allah to please people; and an evil neighbour — if he sees good he buries it, and if he sees evil he broadcasts it. The deed of the believing woman is like that of seventy truthful saints, and the deed of the wicked woman is like the wickedness of a thousand wicked women.""**"
"7434","On the authority of Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Whomever Allah provides with a righteous wife has helped him with half of his religion, so let him fear Allah in the other half.""**"
"7435","On the authority of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""After Islam, a servant gains nothing better for himself than a believing wife — when he looks at her she pleases him, and when he is absent from her she guards him in herself and his wealth.""**"
"7436","On the authority of Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The severest regrets of the sons of Adam are three: a man with irrigated land and a water-camel watering it — when his land thirsts intensely and brings forth its fruit, his camel dies, so he regrets his camel knowing he will find none like it, and regrets his crop spoiling before he can devise a way; a man with a swift horse meeting a host of disbelievers — when the ranks draw near and the enemies of Allah flee, he charges on his horse, but as he is about to overtake, his horse's leg breaks and he dismounts, regretting his horse that he will find none like it, and regretting the victory that had come within reach; and a man with a wife whose appearance and religion please him — she bears a boy then dies in childbed, so he regrets his wife thinking he will never find her like, and regrets for his child fearing its loss before finding one to suckle it. This last is the greatest of these regrets.""**"
"7437","On the authority of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Four — whoever is given them has been given the good of this world and the Hereafter: a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, a body patient under trial, and a wife who seeks no betrayal of him in herself or his wealth.""**"
"7438","On the authority of Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him): > **""O Muadh, a grateful heart, a remembering tongue, and a righteous wife who helps you in your worldly and religious affair are the best of what people earn.""**"
"7439","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Salam (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The best of women is she who pleases you when you look, obeys you when you command, and guards your absence in herself and your wealth.""**"
"7440","On the authority of Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The likeness of the righteous woman among women is that of thewhite-legged crow.""** It was asked: O Messenger of Allah, what is the white-legged crow? He said: > **""The one whose one leg is white.""**"
"7441","Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Amr said: We were with Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) on a Hajj or Umrah, and when we were at Marr al-Zahran there was a woman in her howdah with her hand upon it. When he descended he entered the ravine and we entered with him, and he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at this spot, and there were many crows, among them a crow with a marked beak and leg. He said: > **""None of women will enter Paradise except to the number of that crow among these crows.""** Abu Umar said: Al-asam means red-marked."
"7442","On the authority of Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""The likeness of the believing woman is that of the piebald crow among black crows — without equal or likeness. The likeness of the evil woman is that of a house adorned outwardly and ruined inwardly, like a canopy with no light for it on the Day of Resurrection. By Allah, I fear that no woman rises from her husband's bed turning away from him except while disobedient to Allah and His Messenger.""**"
"7443","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Dawud the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: > **""Be to the orphan as the merciful father, and know that as you sow so shall you reap. The likeness of the righteous wife to her husband is that of a king crowned with gold — whenever he looks at her, his eyes find delight in her. And the likeness of the evil wife to her husband is that of a heavy load upon an aged elder.""**"
"7444","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said: This verse was revealed — And do not marry polytheist women until they believe [2:221] — so the people held back from them until the verse after it was revealed — This day the good things are made lawful for you, and the chaste women of the believers and the chaste women of those given the Book before you [5:5] — whereupon the people married women of the People of the Book."
"7445","On the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Arabs are equals to one another, and clients are equals to one another.""**"
"7446","On the authority of Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: > **""Women are married only to equals, none marries them off but guardians, and there is no dowry below ten dirhams.""**"
"7447","Salmān al-Fārisi رضي الله عنه said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them, meaning the non-Arabs, from marrying Arab women."
"7448","Salmān al-Fārisi رضي الله عنه said concerning the Arabs that they were given precedence by virtue of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying that they would not marry their women."
"7449","Thābit al-Bunāni reported that Abū al-Dardā رضي الله عنه went with Salmān al-Fārisi رضي الله عنه to propose to a woman of Banū Layth on his behalf. He entered and mentioned the virtue of Salmān and his precedence and his Islam, and mentioned that he sought their young woman so-and-so in marriage. They replied that they would not marry Salmān but would marry Abū al-Dardā, so Abū al-Dardā married her and then came out feeling shy to mention what had happened. When Abū al-Dardā informed him of the news, Salmān said that he was more entitled to feel shy toward him for having proposed to her, since Allah had already decreed her for him."
"7450","ʿUrwah reported that ʿAli ibn Abi Tālib رضي الله عنه said to his sons not to send out their daughters except to equals. When they asked who the equals were, he said they were the children of al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām رضي الله عنه."
"7451","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Julaybib, who was unsightly in face, was offered marriage by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he replied that he would then be found unsaleable, the Prophet ﷺ responded: > **""Yet with Allah you are not unsaleable.""**"
"7452","Muʿādh ibn Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ spoke of the reward for restraining anger while able to act upon it and for marrying off a servant: > **""Whoever restrains anger while able to carry it out, Allah will give him choice among the wide-eyed maidens on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever marries off a servant, Allah will place upon his head the crown of kingship on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"7453","Samurah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade encroaching upon a brother's proposal and bargain: > **""No man shall propose over the proposal of his brother, nor shall he bargain over the bargain of his brother.""**"
"7454","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ sent Umm Sulaym رضي الله عنها to look at a slave-girl, instructing her what to inspect: > **""Smell her mouth and look at her ankles.""**"
"7455","Abū Humayd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted looking at a woman for the purpose of proposal even without her knowledge: > **""When one of you proposes to a woman, there is no sin upon him to look at her, when he looks at her only for his proposal, even if she does not know.""**"
"7456","Umm al-Fadl bint al-Hārith رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Umm Habibah bint al-ʿAbbās رضي الله عنها when she was just past weaning. He spoke of marrying her if she reached maturity in his lifetime. She later reached maturity only after he had passed away, and al-Aswad ibn ʿAbd Allah married her and she bore him Rizq ibn al-Aswad and Lubābah bint al-Aswad, whom her grandmother named Umm al-Fadl after herself: > **""If this daughter of al-ʿAbbās reaches maturity while I am alive, I shall surely marry her.""**"
"7457","Saʿd ibn Abi Waqqās رضي الله عنه reported that while he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah he proposed to a woman and wished for someone to see her and inform him about her. A man called Hit offered to describe her, saying that when she approached she walked upon six and when she turned away she walked upon four. The Prophet ﷺ disapproved of this knowledge of women. That man used to enter upon Sawdah رضي الله عنها until the Prophet ﷺ forbade him, then banished him upon arrival in Madinah. He remained so until ʿUmar رضي الله عنه, when he suffered hardship, permitted him to enter Madinah on Fridays to receive charity: > **""I see this as objectionable; I see that he knows the affairs of women.""**"
"7458","ʿAli رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed him concerning his treasure in Paradise and commanded him not to follow one glance with another, with the addition that the second glance is not for him: > **""O ʿAli, you have a treasure in Paradise, and you are Dhū al-Qarnayn. Do not follow one glance with another, for the first is for you, and the latter is not for you.""**"
"7459","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that when Hafsah رضي الله عنها was widowed from Khunays ibn Hudhāfah, ʿUmar رضي الله عنه offered her to ʿUthmān رضي الله عنه, who said he had no need of women but would consider, and then offered her to Abū Bakr رضي الله عنه, who remained silent, which weighed upon ʿUmar. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her. Afterwards ʿUmar met Abū Bakr and said his anger toward Abū Bakr for his silence was greater than toward ʿUthmān for his refusal, and Abū Bakr replied that it had been a secret he disliked to disclose. ʿUmar also complained of ʿUthmān to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who informed him that Hafsah would marry one better than ʿUthmān and ʿUthmān would marry one better than Hafsah, and the Prophet ﷺ then married his own daughter to ʿUthmān رضي الله عنه: > **""One better than ʿUthmān will marry Hafsah, and one better than Hafsah will be married to ʿUthmān.""**"
"7460","Al-Fadl ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a Bedouin with a beautiful daughter alongside him kept presenting her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hoping he would marry her. Whenever al-Fadl turned to look at her, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his head and turned it away, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued chanting the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."
"7461","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wished to marry one of his daughters, he sat beside her curtain and mentioned the names of the man and the girl. If she remained silent he married her off, and if she disliked it she knocked the curtain, in which case he did not marry her off: > **""Indeed so-and-so mentions so-and-so.""**"
"7462","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that when the Prophet ﷺ wished to marry one of his daughters, he sat at her curtain and announced the proposal. Her silence was her permission: > **""Indeed so-and-so proposes to so-and-so. If she remains silent, that is her permission; her silence is her permission.""**"
"7463","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that when one of his daughters received a proposal, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat at the curtain and announced it. Her silence was her approval, and her striking the veil indicated dislike: > **""Indeed so-and-so proposes to so-and-so. If she remains silent, her silence is her approval, and if she dislikes, she strikes the veil, and that is dislike from her.""**"
"7464","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that when a proposal came for one of his daughters, the Prophet ﷺ came to the curtain and announced it. If she struck the curtain he did not marry her off, and if she did not strike it he married her off: > **""Indeed so-and-so proposes to so-and-so. If she strikes the curtain, I shall not marry her off, and if she does not strike it, I shall marry her off.""**"
"7465","ʿUmar رضي الله عنه reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wished to marry a woman of his household, he came to her from behind the veil and instructed her that silence would be consent and that she should say no without shyness if she disliked: > **""O my daughter, so-and-so has proposed to you. If you dislike him, say no, for none feels shy to say no. And if you like him, your silence is consent.""**"
"7466","Muʿāwiyah ibn Hudayj reported that Muʿāwiyah ibn Abi Sufyān sent him to al-Hasan ibn ʿAli to propose for Yazid a daughter or sister of his. Al-Hasan رضي الله عنه replied that they did not marry their women without consulting them. When the messenger mentioned Yazid to the woman, she swore by Allah that it would not happen until his master acted among them as Pharaoh acted among the Children of Israel, slaughtering their sons and sparing their women. When he returned and complained that she had called the Commander of the Believers Pharaoh, al-Hasan warned him against hating them and cited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: > **""None hates us nor envies us except that he will be driven away from the Basin on the Day of Resurrection with whips of fire.""**"
"7467","Ibrāhim ibn Sālih, whose known name was Nuʿaym ibn al-Nahhām, whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had named Sālih, reported through ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما that ʿAbd Allah asked ʿUmar ibn al-Khattāb رضي الله عنه to propose the daughter of Sālih for him. ʿUmar said Sālih had orphans and would not prefer them over them. ʿAbd Allah then sent his uncle Zayd ibn al-Khattāb to propose, and Sālih replied that he had orphans and would not neglect his own flesh to raise another's, and declared before witnesses that he had married her to so-and-so. The girl's mother, whose inclination was toward ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said that ʿAbd Allah had proposed but her father had married her to an orphan in his care without consulting her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to Sālih questioning him, and commanded consultation of women even if virgins. Sālih replied that he had done so only because of what Ibn ʿUmar had given her in charity, claiming for her from his own wealth the like of what he gave: > **""Did you marry your daughter without consulting her? Consult women concerning themselves, even if virgins.""**"
"7468","Abū Mūsā رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ commanded seeking a daughter's permission when marrying her off: > **""When a man wishes to marry off his daughter, let him seek her permission.""**"
"7469","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ distinguished between the virgin, whose permission is silence, and the previously married woman, who decides her affair so long as she does not call to displeasure, in which case if her guardians call to what is pleasing the matter is raised to the ruler: > **""The virgin shall not be married until she is consulted, and her permission is silence. The previously married woman decides her affair so long as she does not call to displeasure; if she calls to displeasure while her guardians call to what is pleasing, that is raised to the ruler.""**"
"7470","Abū Mūsā رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned the affair of women to their fathers and made silence their permission: > **""The affair of women is in the hands of their fathers, and their permission is their silence.""**"
"7471","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rejected the marriage of a previously married woman and a virgin whom their father had married off unwillingly. Al-ʿUrs also reported the command to consult women, with the previously married expressing herself and the virgin's silence being permission: > **""Consult women; the previously married woman expresses herself, and the permission of the virgin is her silence.""**"
"7472","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported that a slave-girl was married off by her father but wished to marry another man. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, so he removed her from the one her father had married her to and the Prophet ﷺ married her to the one she desired."
"7473","ʿAbd al-Rahmān and Mujammiʿ, the sons of Yazid ibn Jāriyah رضي الله عنهم, reported that Hidhām married his daughter to a man while she disliked it and she was previously married. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, so he annulled her marriage."
"7474","Abū Mūsā رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded consulting the orphan girl concerning herself, with silence as permission and refusal preventing compulsion: > **""The orphan girl shall be consulted concerning herself; if she remains silent, she has permitted, and if she refuses, she shall not be compelled.""**"
"7475","ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that when ʿUthmān ibn Mazʿūn رضي الله عنه died, he left a daughter from Khuwaylah bint Hakīm ibn Umayyah ibn Hārithah ibn al-Awqas and entrusted her to his brother Qudāmah ibn Mazʿūn, both maternal uncles of Ibn ʿUmar. Ibn ʿUmar proposed to Qudāmah for the daughter and Qudāmah married her to him. Then al-Mughirah ibn Shuʿbah approached her mother and enticed her with wealth, so she and the girl inclined to the mother's desire and both refused. The matter was raised to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Qudāmah said she was his brother's daughter entrusted to him and he had married her to her cousin ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar without falling short in righteousness or suitability, but she had inclined to her mother. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that she was an orphan not to be married except with her permission. By Allah, after Ibn ʿUmar had possessed her, she was taken from him and married to al-Mughirah ibn Shuʿbah رضي الله عنه: > **""She is an orphan, and she shall not be married except with her permission.""**"
"7476","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded marrying unmarried women, repeating it three times, upon whatever their families mutually agreed, even a handful of arāk: > **""Marry the unmarried women, marry the unmarried women, marry the unmarried women, upon whatever their families mutually agree, even a handful of arāk.""**"
"7477","Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ commanded giving compensation in marriage even if minimal: > **""Compensate them, even with a whip, meaning in marriage.""**"
"7478","Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married a man to a woman for an iron ring whose stone was of silver."
"7479","Husayn ibn ʿAbd Allah ibn Dumayrah, from his father from his grandfather, reported that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him to marry him to so-and-so. The Prophet ﷺ asked what he had to give as dowry and about a ring belonging to him, then commanded him to give it to her and married him to her. He also married another man who had nothing upon Sūrat al-Baqarah: > **""What do you have to give her as dowry? Whose is this ring? Give it to her.""**"
"7480","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the best women are those easiest in dowry: > **""The best of them are those easiest in dowry.""**"
"7481","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the women lightest in dowry are greatest in blessing: > **""The women lightest in dowry are greatest in blessing.""**"
"7482","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said part of a woman's blessedness lies in ease of proposal, ease of dowry, and ease of womb. ʿUrwah added that part of her first ill omen is abundance of her dowry: > **""Part of the blessedness of a woman is ease of her proposal, ease of her dowry, and ease of her womb.""**"
"7483","Yahyā ibn ʿAbd al-Rahmān ibn Abi Labibah, from his father from his grandfather, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one dirham in marriage suffices for lawfulness: > **""Whoever makes lawful with a dirham in marriage has made lawful.""**"
"7484","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ was distributing sheep of charity among his Companions, with one sheep falling between two men. One of them said to leave his share to him so he could marry with it."
"7485","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that ʿAbd al-Rahmān ibn ʿAwf رضي الله عنه married a woman at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the weight of a date-stone of gold, whose value was three dirhams and a third."
"7486","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said he had married a woman of the Ansār. The Prophet ﷺ asked whether he had looked at her since there is something in the eyes of the Ansār, and he replied yes. When asked for how much, he replied four uqiyas, at which the Prophet ﷺ remarked upon its excessiveness: > **""Did you look at her, for in the eyes of the Ansār is something? For how much? For four uqiyas? As though you carve silver from the side of this mountain.""**"
"7487","Abū Hadrad al-Aslami رضي الله عنه reported that he came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking help with a woman's dowry. When asked how much he had fixed, he replied two hundred dirhams, at which the Prophet ﷺ remarked upon its amount: > **""How much did you fix for her? If you scooped from Bathān, you would not have added.""**"
"7488","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ married Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها for household goods whose value was ten dirhams."
"7489","Abū Saʿid al-Khudri رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ married Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها for household goods whose value was ten dirhams."
"7490","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her for household goods worth forty dirhams."
"7491","Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنه reported that Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah رضي الله عنه sent a bowl to the Prophet ﷺ every night. When the Prophet ﷺ proposed to women, he mentioned such-and-such provisions along with the circulating bowl of Saʿd: > **""For you is such-and-such, and the bowl of Saʿd circulates with me wherever I circulate.""**"
"7492","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that al-Najāshi married the Prophet ﷺ to Umm Habibah رضي الله عنها and gave from his own wealth two hundred dinars as dowry."
"7493","Safiyyah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed her and made her freedom her dowry."
"7494","Al-Shaʿbi reported that Juwayriyah رضي الله عنها was owned by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he freed her and made her freedom her dowry, and every captive of Banū al-Mustaliq was freed."
"7495","ʿAli رضي الله عنه reported that he wished to propose to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his daughter but had nothing. Then he recalled his kinship and his care and proposed to him. The Prophet ﷺ asked whether he had anything and about the Hutami armor he had given him on such-and-such day. When ʿAli said it was with him, he commanded him to give it to her, and he gave it to her: > **""Do you have anything? Where is your Hutami armor which I gave you on such-and-such day? Give it to her.""**"
"7496","ʿAli رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married him to his daughter Fātimah رضي الله عنها for an iron Hutami body-armor which he himself had armed him with. He commanded him to send it to her to adorn herself with it, so he sent it to her. By Allah, its price was such-and-such plus four hundred dirhams: > **""Send it to her, that she may adorn herself with it.""**"
"7497","ʿAli رضي الله عنه reported that when he married Fātimah رضي الله عنها he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether to sell his horse or his armor. He commanded him to sell his armor, so he sold it for twelve uqiyas, and that became the dowry of Fātimah: > **""Sell your armor.""**"
"7498","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that when the Prophet ﷺ married ʿAli to Fātimah رضي الله عنهما, he commanded ʿAli not to approach his wife until he presented her something. When ʿAli said he had nothing, he commanded him to give her his Hutami armor. Ibn Abi Rawwād added that the armor was valued at four hundred and eighty dirhams: > **""O ʿAli, do not approach your wife until you present her something. Give her your Hutami armor.""**"
"7499","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that ʿAli رضي الله عنه married Fātimah رضي الله عنها from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a body-armor of iron."
"7500","Zayd ibn Thābit رضي الله عنه reported that ʿAli رضي الله عنه consummated his marriage with Fātimah رضي الله عنها before giving her anything."
"7501","Al-Mughirah ibn Shibl reported that ʿUmar ibn Hurayth proposed to ʿAdi ibn Hātim رضي الله عنه, who said he would marry him only upon his own judgment. When ʿUmar accepted his judgment, ʿAdi said he was not better than the daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and married him for the obligatory dowry."
"7502","Masrūq reported that ʿUmar ibn al-Khattāb رضي الله عنه mounted the minbar of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said that the people had gone to excess in dowries of women, while the dowries between the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions were four hundred dirhams or less. He said that had excess been piety with Allah or honor, they would not have been outstripped to it, and warned that he should not know of a man exceeding four hundred dirhams. Then he descended and a woman of Quraysh confronted him, asking whether he had forbidden exceeding four hundred dirhams. When he said yes, she asked whether he had not heard what Allah revealed in the Qurʾan: And you have given one of them a heap of gold, take nothing from it; would you take it by slander and manifest sin. He said O Allah, forgiveness, all people are more understanding than ʿUmar. Then he returned to the minbar and declared that he had forbidden exceeding four hundred dirhams in women's dowries, but whoever wished to give from his wealth as he loved and whose soul was content might do so."
"7503","Ibn Sirin reported that al-Hasan ibn ʿAli رضي الله عنهما married a woman and sent to her one hundred slave-girls, with each slave-girl a thousand dirhams."
"7504","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها and Makhūl reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distinguished between what makes a woman lawful, which belongs to her, and what honors her father, brother, or guardian after the marriage contract, which belongs to him, with a man most entitled to what honors him through his daughter or sister: > **""Whatever makes the private part of a woman lawful, of dowry or promise, belongs to her. And whatever honors her father or her brother or her guardian after the marriage contract belongs to him, and most entitled to what a man is honored with is his daughter or his sister.""**"
"7505","Suhayb ibn Sinān رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ warned that a man who fixes a dowry while Allah knows he does not intend to pay it, deceiving her by Allah and making her lawful falsely, will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection as an adulterer: > **""Any man who fixes a dowry for a woman, while Allah knows he does not intend to pay it to her, and deceives her by Allah and makes her private part lawful falsely, will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection as an adulterer.""**"
"7506","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said he retained two hadiths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one concerning love of the Ansār and one concerning marrying without intending to fulfill the dowry: > **""Whoever loves the Ansār, Allah loves him. And whoever marries a woman for a dowry while not intending to fulfill it to her is an adulterer.""**"
"7507","Maymūn al-Kurdi, from his father, reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ warn that a man who marries for little or much dowry without intending to render her right, deceives her, then dies without paying her right, will meet Allah as an adulterer: > **""Any man who marries a woman for little or much dowry, with no intention in himself to render her right, deceives her, then dies without rendering her right, will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection as an adulterer.""**"
"7508","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ forbade secret marriage."
"7509","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said that Sunday is a day of wedding and consummation, Monday a day of travel, Tuesday a day of blood, Wednesday a day of taking with no giving in it, Thursday a day of entering upon the ruler, and Friday a day of marriage and union."
"7510","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ promised Paradise for one who combines Friday prayer, fasting that day, visiting the sick, attending a funeral, and attending a wedding: > **""Whoever prays Friday, fasts its day, visits a sick person, attends a funeral, and attends a wedding, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.""**"
"7511","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ restricted marriage to equals and guardians and fixed a minimum dowry: > **""Women shall not be married except from equals, and none shall marry them off except guardians, and there is no dowry less than ten dirhams.""**"
"7512","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ declared void the marriage of a woman without her guardian's permission, affirmed her dowry if consummated, and made the ruler the guardian of one without a guardian: > **""Any woman who marries without permission of a guardian, her marriage is void, her marriage is void. If he has entered with her, she shall have the dowry for what was made lawful of her private part, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian.""**"
"7513","ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ declared void the marriage contracted without the guardian's permission, affirmed her dowry if consummated, commanded separation in either case, and made the ruler the guardian of one without a guardian: > **""Any woman married without permission of her guardian, her marriage is void. If he has entered with her, she shall have her dowry for what was made lawful of her private part, and they shall be separated. If he has not entered with her, they shall be separated, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian.""**"
"7514","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said there is no marriage except with a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of one without a guardian: > **""There is no marriage except with a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian.""**"
"7515","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said marriage requires a guardian: > **""There is no marriage except with a guardian.""**"
"7516","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ required a guardian for marriage and made the ruler the guardian when they disputed: > **""There is no marriage except with a guardian, and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian.""**"
"7517","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ required permission of an upright guardian or a ruler: > **""There is no marriage except with permission of an upright guardian or a ruler.""**"
"7518","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ required a guardian's permission for a woman's marriage: > **""A woman shall not be married except with permission of a guardian.""**"
"7519","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ required a guardian, two witnesses, and a dowry, little or much: > **""There is no marriage except with a guardian, two witnesses, and a dowry, little or much.""**"
"7520","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported in al-Awsat that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ described immoral women as those who marry themselves off, and required a guardian, two witnesses, and a dowry, little or much: > **""The prostitutes are those who marry themselves off. No marriage is valid except with a guardian, two witnesses, and a dowry, little or much.""**"
"7521","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ required a guardian and two just witnesses for marriage: > **""There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses.""**"
"7522","Jabir ibn ʿAbdillah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that there is no valid marriage without a guardian and two just witnesses. > **""There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses.""**"
"7523","ʿAʾishah, radiyallahu ʿanha, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that there is no valid marriage without a guardian and two just witnesses. > **""There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses.""**"
"7524","Abu Musa al-Ashʿari, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that there is no valid marriage without a guardian and two witnesses. > **""There is no marriage except with a guardian and two witnesses.""**"
"7525","ʿImran ibn Husayn, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said that there is no valid marriage without a guardian and two just witnesses. > **""There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses.""**"
"7526","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAbbas, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, said that women have no share in contracting the knot of marriage. Maymunah, radiyallahu ʿanha, entrusted her affair to Umm al-Fadl, radiyallahu ʿanha, and Umm al-Fadl entrusted it to al-ʿAbbas, radiyallahu ʿanhu, and al-ʿAbbas married her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. In another wording, the Prophet ﷺ proposed to Maymunah and her affair was placed with al-ʿAbbas."
"7527","Kardam ibn Qays, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that he went out on a hot day with his cousin Abu Thaʿlabah. Kardam wore sandals and his cousin had none, so his cousin asked for his sandals. Kardam said he would not give them unless his cousin married his daughter to him, and his cousin said he had married her to him. When they returned, his cousin sent back the sandals and said there was no wife for him. The matter was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he told Kardam to leave her, for there was no good in her for him. Kardam then said he had vowed to slaughter a camel from his herd at a certain place, and the Prophet ﷺ told him to fulfil his vow, for there is no vow concerning severing kinship or concerning what the son of Adam does not own. > **""Leave her, there is no good for you in her. Fulfil your vow, for there is no vow in severing kinship nor in what the son of Adam does not own.""**"
"7528","ʿUrwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi reported from Abu Thaʿlabah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, whom he met and spoke with. Abu Thaʿlabah said he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and the Prophet ﷺ said, Nuwaybitah. He asked whether it was a minor matter of good or of evil, and the Prophet ﷺ said it was a minor matter of good. He then told the story of travelling with his uncle, lending sandals in return for marriage to his daughter, and the uncle later returning the sandals and denying the marriage. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said there was no good in her for him, and the rest of the hadith is the same as reported in full in the chapter of lost property. > **""It is rather a minor matter of good. There is no good for you in her.""**"
"7529","Abu al-Dardaʾ, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that in the Age of Ignorance a man would divorce and then take back, saying he was only jesting, and would free a slave and then revoke it, saying he was only jesting. Then Allah revealed, Do not take the verses of Allah in jest. The Prophet ﷺ said that whoever divorces, or declares forbidden, or marries, or gives in marriage, and then says he was only jesting, it is counted as serious. > **""Whoever divorces, or declares unlawful, or marries, or gives in marriage, and says, I was only jesting, then it is serious.""**"
"7530","ʿAbd al-Karim reported that Ibn Masʿud, radiyallahu ʿanhu, said that whoever marries in jest or divorces in jest, it is valid and takes effect."
"7531","ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach them the sermon of need, saying, All praise belongs to Allah, we praise Him, seek His help, and seek refuge with Allah from the evils of our souls and the evils of our deeds. Whomever Allah guides none can misguide, and whomever He misguides none can guide. I bear witness that none is worthy of worship but Allah alone without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Abu ʿUbaydah reported that he heard Abu Musa, radiyallahu ʿanhu, say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say, If you wish you may add verses of the Qurʾan, Fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims, and Fear Allah through Whom you ask one another and the wombs, indeed Allah is Watchful over you, and Fear Allah and speak upright words, He will amend your deeds and forgive your sins, and whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has attained great success. Then, Amma baʿd, speak of your need. > **""All praise belongs to Allah, we praise Him and seek His help and seek refuge with Allah from the evils of our souls and the evils of our deeds. Whomever Allah guides none can misguide, and whomever He misguides none can guide. I bear witness that none is worthy of worship but Allah alone without partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.""**"
"7532","ʿAli al-Sulami, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said to him, Shall I not marry you to Umaymah the daughter of Rabiʿah ibn al-Harith. He said yes, and the Prophet ﷺ said he had married her to him. > **""Shall I not marry you to Umaymah the daughter of Rabiʿah ibn al-Harith. I have married her to you.""**"
"7533","Abu Hasan, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Prophet ﷺ disliked secret marriage until the duff is beaten and it is said, We have come to you, we have come to you, greet us and we greet you. > **""We have come to you, we have come to you, so greet us and we greet you.""**"
"7534","ʿAbdullah ibn al-Zubayr, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said to announce the marriage openly. > **""Announce the marriage.""**"
"7535","Jabir, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAʾishah, radiyallahu ʿanha, Did you escort the girl to her house. She said yes. He asked why they did not send with her one who would sing, We have come to you, we have come to you, greet us and we greet you, for the Ansar are a people in whom there is fondness for poetry. > **""Did you escort the girl to her house. Why did you not send with her one who sings, We have come to you, we have come to you, greet us and we greet you, for the Ansar are a people in whom there is fondness for poetry.""**"
"7536","The husband of the daughter of Abu Lahab reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them when he married the daughter of Abu Lahab and asked whether there was any amusement. > **""Is there any amusement.""**"
"7537","ʿAʾishah, radiyallahu ʿanha, reported that the Prophet ﷺ asked what happened to a certain orphan girl under her care. She said she had escorted her to her husband. He asked whether they sent with her a girl to beat the duff and sing. She asked what she should say, and he told her to say, We have come to you, we have come to you, greet us and we greet you. Were it not for red gold she would not have settled in your valley. Were it not for brown wheat your virgins would not have grown plump. > **""Did you send with her a girl to beat the duff and sing, We have come to you, we have come to you, greet us and we greet you. Were it not for red gold she would not have settled in your valley. Were it not for brown wheat your virgins would not have grown plump.""**"
"7538","Anas ibn Malik, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that when the Prophet ﷺ first arrived in Madinah he passed a bride with women, and one of them was singing, He presented to her a ram wallowing in the enclosure, and your husband is in the desert and knows what tomorrow holds. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said not to say that, but to say, We have come to you, we have come to you, greet us and we greet you. > **""Do not say this, but say, We have come to you, we have come to you, greet us and we greet you.""**"
"7539","ʿAʾishah, radiyallahu ʿanha, reported that the Prophet ﷺ passed women of the Ansar at a wedding singing, He presented to her a ram wallowing in the enclosure, and your husband is in the desert and knows what tomorrow holds. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that none knows what tomorrow holds except Allah. > **""None knows what tomorrow holds except Allah.""**"
"7540","Al-Saʾib ibn Yazid, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met slave girls singing, Greet us and we greet you. He stopped for them and called them and said not to say that, but to say, May Allah greet us and you. A man asked whether he permitted people this, and he said yes, for it is marriage not fornication, so proclaim marriage with song. > **""Do not say this, but say, May Allah greet us and you. Yes, it is marriage not fornication, so proclaim the marriage.""**"
"7541","ʿAbdullah ibn Habbar reported from his father Habbar, radiyallahu ʿanhu, that Habbar married his daughter and the kir and the ghirbal were beaten at her wedding. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard it and asked what it was. They said Habbar had married his daughter and the kir and ghirbal were beaten at her wedding. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to proclaim the marriage twice, for this is marriage not fornication. > **""Proclaim the marriage, proclaim the marriage, this is marriage not fornication.""**"
"7542","Muʿadh ibn Jabal, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that he attended the marriage of a man of the Ansar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the sermon and married the Ansari, and said, Upon affection and good and blessed fortune, beat the duff over your companion. They beat the duff over his head, and baskets of fruit and sugar came and were scattered over them, but the people held back and did not take. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said how beautiful is forbearance, why do you not take. They said he had forbidden plunder on such and such day. He said he had forbidden the plunder of armies, not the sharing of wedding feasts, so take. Muʿadh said he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pulling it and pulling them toward that sharing. In another wording he said, Upon good and blessing and affection and blessed fortune and abundance in provision, may Allah bless you. > **""Upon affection and good and blessed fortune, beat the duff over your companion. I only forbade you the plunder of armies, and I did not forbid you the sharing of wedding feasts, so take.""**"
"7543","Jabir, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that a woman quarrelling with her husband came with him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The woman said, This is my husband, by the One Who sent you with truth, there is none on earth more hateful to me than he. The husband said, This is my wife, by the One Who sent you with truth, there is none on earth more hateful to me than she. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to come near him and supplicated for them, and they did not leave him until the woman said, By the One Who sent you with truth, Allah has created nothing more beloved to me than he, and the husband said, By the One Who sent you with truth, Allah has created nothing more beloved to me than she. > **""Come near to me.""**"
"7544","Ibn ʿAbbas, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that Salman, radiyallahu ʿanhu, returned from an absence and ʿUmar, radiyallahu ʿanhu, met him and said, May Allah be pleased with you as a servant. Salman then married in Kindah, and on the night he was to enter upon his family the house was furnished and women were present. He asked whether the Kaʿbah had moved to Kindah or whether this was vanity, for his intimate friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ had commanded them to take of goods only like the provision of a traveller, and of women only those they marry. The women left, and he entered upon his wife and said, O woman, will you obey me or disobey me. She said she would obey him in whatever he wished. He said his intimate friend ﷺ had commanded them that when one of them enters upon his wife he should stand and pray and command her to pray behind him, and he should supplicate and she should say amin. He and she did so. When he sat in the gathering of Kindah a man asked, How are you O Abu ʿAbdillah, how did you find your wife. He remained silent, and when asked again he said, What is it with one of you that he asks about what walls and doors have veiled, it suffices one of you to ask about a matter, if he is answered well, and if he is met with silence, that is well."
"7545","Salman, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that when one of you marries and the night of consummation comes, he should pray two rakʿahs and command his wife to pray behind him, for Allah will place good in the house. > **""When one of you marries and the night of consummation comes, let him pray two rakʿahs and command her to pray behind him, for Allah will place good in the house.""**"
"7546","Ibn Masʿud, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said that when the wife enters upon her husband, the man should stand and she should stand behind him, and they should pray two rakʿahs and say, O Allah, bless me in my family and bless my family in me, O Allah, provide them through me and provide me through them, O Allah, join us together as long as You join in good, and separate us when You separate toward good. > **""When the wife enters upon her husband, the man stands and she stands behind him, and they pray two rakʿahs and say, O Allah, bless me in my family and bless my family in me, O Allah, provide them through me and provide me through them, O Allah, join us together as long as You join in good, and separate us when You separate toward good.""**"
"7547","Abu Waʾil reported that a man of Bajilah came to ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, radiyallahu ʿanhu, and said he had married a virgin girl and feared she would hate him. ʿAbdullah said affection is from Allah and hatred is from Satan, who seeks to make hateful what Allah has made lawful. When he enters upon her he should command her to pray two rakʿahs behind him. Al-Aʿmash mentioned it to Ibrahim, who added that ʿAbdullah said to say, O Allah, bless me in my family and bless them in me, O Allah, provide them through me and provide me through them, O Allah, join us together as long as You join toward good, and separate us when You separate toward good. > **""Affection is from Allah, and hatred is from Satan, who seeks to make hateful what Allah has made lawful. When you enter upon her, command her to pray two rakʿahs behind you.""**"
"7548","Muʿawiyah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him not to approach his wife at the beginning of the crescent, not to perform ablution from copper, and to use the tooth-stick whenever he rose from sleep. > **""Do not approach your wife at the beginning of the crescent, do not perform ablution from copper, and use the tooth-stick whenever you rise from sleep.""**"
"7549","Abu Kabshah al-Anmari, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat with his Companions, then entered and came out having bathed. When asked whether something had happened, he said yes, a certain woman passed by him and desire for women fell in his heart, so he went to one of his wives and approached her. Likewise the protection among the best of your deeds is approaching the lawful. In another wording he said to do likewise. > **""Yes, a woman passed by me and desire for women fell in my heart, so I went to one of my wives and approached her. Likewise do, for approaching the lawful is among the best protection of your deeds.""**"
"7550","Anas, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that there was a perfumer woman in Madinah, then he mentioned the hadith from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the virtue of a man approaching his wife in marriage."
"7551","Ibn ʿUmar, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that the Prophet ﷺ asked a man of his Companions whether he had visited a sick person today, given charity, prayed over a funeral, or approached his wife. The man said no to each, and the Prophet ﷺ told him to approach them, for it is charity from him upon them. That was on a Friday. > **""Did you visit a sick person today. Did you give charity. Did you pray over a funeral. Did you approach your wife. Then approach them, for it is charity from you upon them.""**"
"7552","Abu Umamah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that none of you should be unable, when he approaches his wife, to say, In the name of Allah, O Allah, keep me away and keep what You provide me away from the accursed Satan. If a child is decreed between them, Satan will never harm him. > **""When one of you approaches his wife, let him say, In the name of Allah, O Allah, keep me away and keep what You provide me away from the accursed Satan, for if a child is decreed between them, Satan will never harm him.""**"
"7553","Jabir, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given al-kafīt. When al-Hasan was asked what al-kafīt is, he said it means vigour. Ibn al-Athir said al-kafīt means intercourse."
"7554","Ibn ʿUmar, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, said he was given something of vigour which he knew none was given except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, meaning intercourse."
"7555","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he was given the strength of forty in grip and in marriage, and every believer is given the strength of ten. Desire was made in ten parts, nine tenths in women and one in men. Were it not for the modesty cast upon them along with their desires, every man would have nine ardent wives. > **""I was given the strength of forty in grip and in marriage, and every believer is given the strength of ten. Desire was made in ten parts, nine tenths in women and one in men. Were it not for the modesty cast upon them along with their desires, every man would have nine ardent wives.""**"
"7556","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the excess of the pleasure of the woman over the pleasure of the man is like the mark of a needle in clay, except that Allah veils them with modesty. > **""The excess of the pleasure of the woman over the pleasure of the man is like the mark of a needle in clay, except that Allah veils them with modesty.""**"
"7557","Abu Hurayrah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that when one of you approaches his wife he should cover, for if he does not cover the angels are shy and leave, and if a child is between them Satan will have a share in him. > **""When one of you approaches his wife, let him cover, for if he does not cover the angels are shy and leave, and if a child is between them Satan will have a share in him.""**"
"7558","ʿAbdullah ibn Masʿud, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that when one of you approaches his wife he should cover and not strip naked like two donkeys stripping. > **""When one of you approaches his wife, let him cover, and let him not strip naked like two donkeys.""**"
"7559","Abu Umamah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that when one of you approaches his wife he should cover himself and his wife, and they should not strip naked like donkeys. > **""When one of you approaches his wife, let him cover himself and his wife, and let them not strip naked like donkeys.""**"
"7560","Abu Umamah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat one day with a woman present, he said he thought women disclose what their husbands do with them. She swore by her father and mother that they do so. He said not to do so, for Allah detests whoever does that. He said he thought that when her husband comes to one of them they cast off the blanket and look at one another's nakedness like two donkeys. She swore they do so, and he said not to do so, for Allah detests that. > **""Do not do so, for Allah detests whoever does that. Do not do so, for Allah detests that.""**"
"7561","Saʿd ibn Masʿud al-Laythi, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that ʿUthman ibn Mazʿun, radiyallahu ʿanhu, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said he was shy that his wife should see his nakedness. The Prophet ﷺ asked why, since Allah made him a garment for them and them a garment for him. He said he disliked it. The Prophet ﷺ said they see it from him and he sees it from them. He asked, Are you the Messenger of Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said yes. He asked who then after him. When ʿUthman turned away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that Ibn Mazʿun is modest and veiling. > **""Why, when Allah has made you a garment for them and them a garment for you. They see it from me and I see it from them. Ibn Mazʿun is modest and veiling.""**"
"7562","Asmaʾ bint Yazid, radiyallahu ʿanha, reported that she was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while men and women sat with him. He said perhaps a man mentions what he does with his wife, and perhaps a woman informs of what she did with her husband. The people fell silent, and she said by Allah they do so. He said not to do so, for it is like a devil meeting a she-devil and covering her while people look on. > **""Perhaps a man mentions what he does with his wife, and perhaps a woman informs of what she did with her husband. Do not do so, for it is like a devil meeting a she-devil and covering her while people look on.""**"
"7563","Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported from the Prophet ﷺ that perhaps one of you is alone with his wife behind a closed door and lowered curtain, fulfils his need, then goes out and tells his companions of that, and perhaps one of you women closes her door and lowers her curtain, fulfils her need, then tells her companions. A woman with yellowish cheeks said by Allah they do so. He said not to do so, for it is like a devil meeting a she-devil on the roadside, fulfilling his need from her, then turning away and leaving her. > **""Do not do so, for it is like a devil meeting a she-devil on the roadside, fulfilling his need from her, then turning away and leaving her.""**"
"7564","Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported from the Prophet ﷺ that al-shibaʿ is forbidden. Ibn Lahiʿah said it means one who boasts of intercourse. Ibn al-Athir said it is al-sibaʿ with sin or with shin. > **""Al-shibaʿ is forbidden.""**"
"7565","Wathilah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to the wife under him that calmness and dignity be upon her. > **""Upon you be calmness and dignity.""**"
"7566","Anas ibn Malik, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that when one of you has intercourse with his wife he should be sincere to her, and if he fulfils his need before she fulfils hers, he should not hasten her until she fulfils her need. > **""When one of you has intercourse with his wife, let him be sincere to her, and if he fulfils his need before she fulfils hers, let him not hasten her until she fulfils her need.""**"
"7567","ʿUmar, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported from the Prophet ﷺ that when one of you approaches his wife and then wishes to return, he should wash his private part. > **""When one of you approaches his wife, then wishes to return, let him wash his private part.""**"
"7568","Talq ibn ʿAli, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that when one of you desires his wife for a need, he should come to her even if she is at the oven. In the wording of al-Tirmidhi, when a man calls his wife for his need she should come to him even if she is at the oven. > **""When one of you desires his wife for a need, let him come to her even if she is at the oven.""**"
"7569","Muhammad ibn Sirin reported that a labourer of Anas ibn Malik, radiyallahu ʿanhu, who worked on a zurnuq, was complained against by his wife to Anas that he did not leave her night or day. Anas reconciled between them upon six times in each day and night."
"7570","Abu Hurayrah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the musawwifah and the mufassilah. As for the musawwifah, she is the one who when her husband desires her says, Later, now. As for the mufassilah, she is the one who when her husband desires her says, I am menstruating, while she is not menstruating. > **""Allah curses the musawwifah and the mufassilah.""**"
"7571","Ibn ʿUmar, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, May Allah curse the musawwifat. It was said, O Prophet of Allah, who are the musawwifat. He said, She whose husband calls her to his bed and she says, Later, until sleep overcomes him. > **""May Allah curse the musawwifat. She whose husband calls her to his bed and she says, Later, until sleep overcomes him.""**"
"7572","Ibn ʿUmar, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that there is no woman whose husband seeks his need from her and she refuses, so he spends the night angry with her, except that she spends the night with the angels cursing her until morning. > **""There is no woman whose husband seeks his need from her and she refuses, so he spends the night angry with her, except that the angels curse her until morning.""**"
"7573","Anas ibn Malik, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking about withdrawal. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that if the fluid from which a child is to be were poured upon a rock, Allah would bring forth a child from it, and Allah will create every soul He is to create. > **""If the fluid from which a child is to be were poured upon a rock, Allah would bring forth a child from it, and Allah will create every soul He is to create.""**"
"7574","ʿUbadah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the first who practised withdrawal were men of the Ansar. They came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said some of the Ansar practise withdrawal. He was alarmed and said the created soul will come to be, so he neither commands nor forbids. > **""The created soul will come to be, so I neither command nor forbid.""**"
"7575","Ibn ʿAbbas, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if the drop upon which Allah took the covenant were cast upon a rock, Allah would create a human from it. > **""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if the drop upon which Allah took the covenant were cast upon a rock, Allah would create a human from it.""**"
"7576","Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that they were discussing withdrawal and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard them and came out to them and said, Do you do it. They said yes. He said, Do you not know that Allah never creates a soul He fashions except that it will come to be. > **""Do you do it. Do you not know that Allah never creates a soul He fashions except that it will come to be.""**"
"7577","Sirmah al-ʿUdhri, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided Banu Sulaym and they took noble Arab women. They desired sale and were pressed by bachelorhood, so they wished to enjoy and withdraw. Some said they should not do that while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among them until they asked him. They asked him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to withdraw or not withdraw, whatever soul Allah has written to come to be till the Day of Resurrection will come to be. > **""Withdraw or do not withdraw, whatever soul Allah has written to come to be till the Day of Resurrection will come to be.""**"
"7578","Wathilah ibn al-Asqaʿ, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that men of Banu Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and said they obtain captives and withdraw from them. He asked whether they do so, they said yes, and he said whatever soul Allah wishes to emerge from the loins of a man will emerge whether he wishes or refuses, so it is no harm upon you not to do it. > **""Do you do so. Whatever soul Allah wishes to emerge from the loins of a man will emerge whether he wishes or refuses, so it is no harm upon you not to do it.""**"
"7579","Ibn Masʿud, radiyallahu ʿanhu, said that if Allah took a covenant upon a soul in the loins of a man, then it were cast upon Safa, He would bring it forth from that Safa. If you wish complete, and if you wish do not withdraw."
"7580","Zaʾidah ibn ʿUmayr al-Taʾi said he asked Ibn ʿAbbas, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, about withdrawal. He said whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about it is as he said, and otherwise he says, Your wives are a field for you, come to your field as you wish. Whoever wishes may withdraw and whoever wishes may leave it."
"7581","Abu Hurayrah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Jews used to say withdrawal is the minor burial alive. That reached the Prophet ﷺ and he said the Jews lied, for if Allah wishes to create a creation nothing prevents Him. > **""The Jews lied, for if Allah wishes to create a creation nothing prevents Him.""**"
"7582","Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, radiyallahu ʿanhu, said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that the Jews say withdrawal is the minor burial alive. He said the Jews lied. > **""The Jews lied.""**"
"7583","Ibn Masʿud, radiyallahu ʿanhu, said concerning withdrawal that it is the hidden minor burial alive, and he later returned from that view."
"7584","Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that ʿUmar and Ibn ʿUmar, radiyallahu ʿanhum, disliked withdrawal, while Zayd and Ibn Masʿud, radiyallahu ʿanhum, practised withdrawal."
"7585","Jarir, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said he obtained nothing from the polytheists except a slave girl whom he intended for the market, and asked whether he should withdraw from her. He said what is decreed for her will come to her. > **""What is decreed for her will come to her.""**"
"7586","ʿAli ibn al-Hasan reported from his grandmother that al-Hasan ibn ʿAli, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, used to practise withdrawal with her, and she was his concubine."
"7587","Salman, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that whoever takes servants other than by marriage, then they commit immorality, upon him is the like of their sins without diminishing their sins in anything. > **""Whoever takes servants other than by marriage, then they commit immorality, upon him is the like of their sins without diminishing their sins in anything.""**"
"7588","Habashi ibn Junadah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that withholding is a form of injustice. > **""Withholding is a form of injustice.""**"
"7589","Ibn ʿAbbas, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade ightiyal, then said if it harmed anyone it would harm Persia and Rome. Ibn Bukayr said ightiyal is a man approaching his wife while she nurses. > **""If it harmed anyone it would harm Persia and Rome.""**"
"7590","Abu Hurayrah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade ghayl, then said it did not harm Persia and Rome. That is a man approaching his wife while she nurses. > **""It did not harm Persia and Rome.""**"
"7591","ʿAbdullah ibn ʿAmr, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that the Prophet ﷺ said it is the minor sodomy, meaning a man approaching his wife in her posterior. > **""It is the minor sodomy.""**"
"7592","ʿUmar, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to be modest, for Allah is not shy of truth, and not to approach women in their posteriors. > **""Be modest, for Allah is not shy of truth, and do not approach women in their posteriors.""**"
"7593","ʿAli ibn Abi Talib, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said they are in the desert and slight wind passes from one of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said Allah is not shy of truth, when one of you does that he should perform ablution, and not approach women in their posteriors. Once he said in their backs. > **""Allah is not shy of truth, when one of you does that let him perform ablution, and do not approach women in their posteriors.""**"
"7594","Jabir ibn ʿAbdillah, radiyallahu ʿanhuma, reported that the Prophet ﷺ forbade the posteriors of women. > **""Do not approach the posteriors of women.""**"
"7595","ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmir, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that Allah curses those who approach women in their posteriors. > **""May Allah curse those who approach women in their posteriors.""**"
"7596","Abu Hurayrah, radiyallahu ʿanhu, reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that whoever approaches women in their posteriors has disbelieved. > **""Whoever approaches women in their posteriors has disbelieved.""**"
"7597","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) warned against intercourse with a menstruating wife and linked heedlessness in it to blame and harm for any child decreed from it. > **""Whoever has intercourse with a woman while she is menstruating, and a child is decreed between them, and leprosy afflicts him, let him blame no one but himself.""**"
"7598","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) confessing that he had approached his wife while she was menstruating, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded him to free a slave, whose value at that time was a dinar."
"7599","Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked what is lawful for a man of his menstruating wife, and he defined the limit by the waist-wrapper. > **""What is above the waist-wrapper, and what is beneath the waist-wrapper of her is forbidden.""**"
"7600","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) disowned the act of approaching a woman pregnant by another man. > **""He is not from us who has intercourse with a pregnant woman.""**"
"7601","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade any man to approach a woman whose pregnancy belongs to another. > **""No man should ever have intercourse with a woman whose pregnancy belongs to another.""**"
"7602","Yahya ibn Said ibn Dinar, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, conveyed from a trustworthy source that on the day of Khaybar the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade approaching pregnant women and likened it to watering another man's field. > **""Would you water another man's crop?""**"
"7603","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that on the day of Khaybar the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade intercourse with pregnant women until they delivered."
"7604","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) declare every pregnant slave girl forbidden to her owner until she delivers. > **""Every slave girl who is pregnant is forbidden to her owner until she delivers what is in her womb.""**"
"7605","Raja ibn Haywah reported from his father from his grandfather that a heavily pregnant slave girl from Khaybar passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He asked whose she was and whether her master approached her, then warned of the confusion of lineage and enslavement of a nourished child. > **""How will he deal with her child — will he claim him though he is not his son, or will he enslave him while he nourished his hearing and sight? I had intended to curse him with a curse that would enter the grave with him.""**"
"7606","Jamil ibn Zayd said he accompanied an Ansari companion, Kab ibn Zayd or Zayd ibn Kab, who told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married a woman of Banu Ghifar. When he sat on the bed and saw whiteness on her side, he withdrew and took nothing of what he had given. > **""Keep your clothes on you.""**"
"7607","Jamil ibn Zayd reported from Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married a woman of Banu Ghifar, saw whiteness on her side when he entered upon her, sent her back, and blamed concealment. > **""You have deceived me.""**"
"7608","Sahl ibn Sad (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married a Bedouin woman, found whiteness on her, and separated from her before consummation."
"7609","Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled that an impotent husband is granted a year. If he consummates the marriage within it, well and good; otherwise separation is made between them, and the wife keeps her dower."
"7610","Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him, may Allah be pleased with her), said she was visited by Khuwaylah bint Hakim, wife of Uthman ibn Mazun, in neglected appearance. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked why, Aishah explained that Khuwaylah's husband fasted by day and prayed by night and neglected her. He summoned Uthman and corrected excess in worship. > **""O Uthman, have you turned away from my Sunnah? I sleep and pray, fast and break fast, and marry women. Fear Allah, O Uthman, for your family has a right over you, your guest has a right over you, and your self has a right over you. So fast and break fast, pray and sleep.""**"
"7611","In another narration from Ahmad, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) denied monasticism and affirmed himself as the most God-fearing guardian of limits. In a further narration, Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said Uthman ibn Mazun's wife abandoned adornment because her husband renounced the world and women. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) met Uthman and called him to his example. > **""Monasticism was not prescribed for us. The most God-fearing of you and the most observant of His limits am I. Do you believe in what we believe in? Then why do you not follow my example?""**"
"7612","Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that Uthman ibn Mazun's wife came to the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in poor appearance and complained that her wealthy husband fasted by day and prayed by night and neglected her. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) admonished Uthman, after which she returned perfumed like a bride and said she received what people receive. > **""O Uthman, do you not have an example in me? You pray by night and fast by day, yet your family has a right over you and your body has a right over you. So pray and sleep, fast and break fast.""**"
"7613","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) saw Uthman ibn Mazun's wife neglected though she used to adorn herself for her husband, because Uthman with Ali ibn Abi Talib and Abdullah ibn Rawahah had withdrawn for worship, abandoned women and meat, and kept vigil and fast. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to them and rejected innovated monasticism. > **""I was only sent with the upright, easy religion, and I was not sent with innovated monasticism. Peoples innovated monasticism and it was imposed upon them, yet they did not observe it duly. So eat meat, approach women, fast and break fast, pray and sleep, for I was commanded with that.""**"
"7614","Al-Miqdam ibn Madikarib (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among the people, praised Allah, and twice enjoined kindness to women, naming mothers, daughters, and maternal aunts, and noting how even a man of the People of the Book who marries a poor woman remains attached to her. > **""Allah enjoins you to treat women well. Allah enjoins you to treat women well, for they are your mothers, your daughters, and your maternal aunts. A man of the People of the Book marries a woman whose hands barely hold a thread, yet neither turns away from the other.""**"
"7615","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) linked completeness of faith to character and kindness to wives. > **""The most complete of believers in faith are the best of them in character, and the best of them to their wives.""**"
"7616","Abu Kabshah (may Allah be pleased with him) said he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) define the best men by conduct to their families. > **""The best of you are the best of you to their families.""**"
"7617","Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) defined the best men by conduct to their families. > **""The best of you are the best of you to their families.""**"
"7618","Abdur Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) defined the best men by conduct to their families and named himself foremost in it. > **""The best of you are the best of you to their families, and I am the best of you to my family.""**"
"7619","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that excellence is measured by treatment of wives. > **""The best of you are the best of you to their wives.""**"
"7620","Al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) condemned beating a wife as a slave is beaten and set kindness as the measure of excellence. > **""It may be that one of you beats his wife as a slave is beaten. Nay, the best of you are the best of you to their families.""**"
"7621","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had permitted disciplining wives, then heard loud voices by night. When told this followed the permission, he reaffirmed kindness as the measure of excellence and named himself foremost. > **""The best of you are the best of you to their families, and I am the best of you to my family.""**"
"7622","Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) defined the best men by conduct to their families. > **""The best of you are the best of you to their families.""**"
"7623","Nuaym ibn Qanab said he went to al-Rabadhah and found Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) exchanging words with his wife, each repeating upon the other. Abu Dharr then cited the Prophet's (peace and blessings be upon him) description of women. > **""Woman is like a rib. If you try to straighten her, she will break, yet in her there is sufficiency and crookedness.""**"
"7624","Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) likened woman to a rib that breaks if straightened and is enjoyed despite crookedness. > **""Woman is like a rib. If you set her straight, you will break her, yet she is enjoyed with her crookedness.""**"
"7625","A man reported that he heard Samurah preaching on the pulpit of Basrah, saying he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) describe woman's creation from a rib and command gentle management. > **""Woman was created from a rib. If you seek to straighten the rib, you will break it. So treat her gently and you will live with her.""**"
"7626","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said a woman will never remain straight upon one disposition, likened her to a rib, and in one narration explained breaking as divorce. > **""Woman will never be straight for you upon one disposition. She is only like a rib. If you straighten her, you will break her, and if you leave her, you will enjoy her, though crookedness remains in her. And her breaking is her divorce.""**"
"7627","A shaykh reported from his father that Jarir ibn Abdullah complained to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) of trouble from women. Umar said he found the same, even being accused of seeking other girls when leaving for a need. Abdullah ibn Masud then recalled that Ibrahim (peace be upon him) complained of Sarah's temperament and was told she was created from a rib, so live with her as she is unless disgrace appears in her religion. Umar praised his knowledge."
"7628","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that women came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said men had taken excellence through jihad, asking what deed would let them reach fighters. He answered with household care. > **""The work of one of you in her house attains the deeds of the fighters in the path of Allah.""**"
"7629","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that Sallamah, nurse of Ibrahim son of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), asked why men receive all glad tidings and not women. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked if her companions sent her, then detailed reward for pregnancy with a pleased husband, labor, delivery, nursing sips, and sleepless nights, for grateful obedient women. > **""Would not one of you be pleased that when she is pregnant by her husband while he is pleased with her, she has the reward of one who fasts and prays in the path of Allah, and when labor comes no dweller of heaven or earth knows what comfort is hidden for her, and when she delivers no sip of milk nor suck but brings her a good deed for every sip and suck, and if she stays awake a night she has the reward of freeing seventy slaves in the path of Allah? I mean by this the favored, righteous, obedient women who are not ungrateful to their companions.""**"
"7630","Said ibn Jubayr reported from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), thinking it raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that a woman from pregnancy to delivery to end of nursing is like one guarding the frontier in Allah's path, and death in between brings a martyr's reward. > **""A woman, from her pregnancy to her delivery to the end of her nursing, is like one guarding the frontier in the path of Allah, and if she dies in between, she has the reward of a martyr.""**"
"7631","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) as envoy of women, saying Allah ordained jihad for men with reward or living martyrdom while women serve them, and asked their share. He sent her back with a message. > **""Convey to the women you meet that obedience to the husband and acknowledgment of his right equals that, though few of you do it.""**"
"7632","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) promised Paradise to a woman who prays her five, fasts her month, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband. > **""When a woman prays her five, fasts her month, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, she will enter Paradise.""**"
"7633","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that a man seeking jihad was forbidden by his mother, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) told him to remain with her for like reward. Another man vowed to sacrifice himself, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered a hundred camels over three years as fulfillment. Then a woman envoy asked what obedience equals men's jihad. > **""Stay with your mother, for you have with her reward like yours in jihad. Obedience to their husbands and recognition of their rights, though few of you do it.""**"
"7634","Abdur Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said a woman who prays her five, fasts her month, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband will be invited to any gate of Paradise. > **""When a woman prays her five, fasts her month, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, it will be said to her: Enter through whichever gates of Paradise you wish.""**"
"7635","Abdur Rahman ibn Hasanah (may Allah be pleased with him) said he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) promise entry through any gate of Paradise to a woman who fasts her month, prays her five, obeys her husband, and guards her chastity. > **""When a woman fasts her month, prays her five, obeys her husband, and guards her chastity, let her enter through whichever gates of Paradise she wishes.""**"
"7636","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that a God-fearing, chaste, obedient wife will find eight gates of Paradise opened to her. > **""Any woman who fears her Lord, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, eight gates of Paradise will be opened for her, and it will be said to her: Enter from wherever you wish.""**"
"7637","Husayn ibn Mihsan reported that his paternal aunt came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He asked if she was married, how she stood with her husband, and she said she falls short only in what she cannot do. He warned of her husband's station. > **""Are you married? Where do you stand with him? You fall short in nothing but what you cannot do? Then see how you are to him, for he is your Paradise and your Fire.""**"
"7638","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that a widowed woman of Khatham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for a husband's rights, saying she would marry only if able. He listed immediate response even on a camel's back, no voluntary fast or leaving home without permission, and curses of angels until return. She vowed never to marry. > **""A husband's right over his wife is that if he asks her for himself while she is on a camel's back, she should not refuse him. Of his right is that she not fast voluntarily except with his permission, else she only hungers and thirsts without acceptance, and not leave her house except with his permission, else angels of heaven, mercy, and punishment curse her until she returns.""**"
"7639","Abu Said al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that a man brought his daughter who refused marriage. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) told her to obey her father, but she swore she would not marry until told a husband's right. He described licking wounds or swallowing pus and blood without fulfilling it. She swore never to marry, and he ordered marriage only with permission. > **""A husband's right over his wife is such that if he had a wound and she licked it, or his nostrils flowed with pus or blood and she swallowed it, she would not fulfill his right. Do not marry them except with their permission.""**"
"7640","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that a woman calling herself daughter of so-and-so asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for a husband's right before accepting a suitor. He mentioned licking flowing blood and pus without fulfilling it and the hypothetical command of prostration. She swore never to marry. > **""Of a husband's right over his wife is that if his nostrils flowed with blood and pus and she licked it, she would not fulfill his right. If it were fitting for a human to prostrate to a human, I would have commanded a wife to prostrate to her husband when he comes to her.""**"
"7641","Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) for a husband's right. He answered with the image of a leprous, discharging husband licked by the tongue without fulfilling his right, and forbade leaving home or spending from it without permission. > **""If a woman left her house then returned to find her husband broken with leprosy, his nose flowing, and she licked him with her tongue, she would not fulfill his right. No wife may leave her husband's house nor give from his house except with his permission.""**"
"7642","Aidhullah ibn Abdullah Abu Idris al-Khawlani reported that Muadh (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Yemen and was met by a Khawlan woman with twelve sons, holding two by the arms, who asked who sent him. When he said the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent him, she adjured him to state a man's right over his wife. He first urged piety and obedience, then swore the enormity of the right. > **""By the One in Whose Hand is Muadh's soul, if you returned to him to find leprosy had eaten his flesh and torn his nostrils, and you found them flowing with pus and blood, then you took them into your mouth to reach his right, you would never reach it at all.""**"
"7643","Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said a woman cannot fulfill Allah's right until she fulfills her husband's, even if summoned on a camel's saddle. > **""A woman does not fulfill Allah's right over her until she fulfills her husband's right, even if he asks her while she is on a camel's saddle, she should not refuse him.""**"
"7644","Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among men and women, told women to repeat the Abyssinian caller's adhan for a thousand thousand degrees per letter, told Umar men have double, then described the obedient faithful wife one degree from martyrs in Paradise and wedded in Paradise to a believer husband or to martyrs. > **""O assembly of women, when you hear this Abyssinian's call and its establishment, repeat what he says, for you have for every letter a thousand thousand degrees. Double, O Umar. No woman obeys, fulfills her husband's right, remembers his good, and betrays him not in herself or his wealth, but she stands one degree from the martyrs in Paradise. If her husband is a believer of good character, she is his wife in Paradise; otherwise Allah will marry her to the martyrs.""**"
"7645","Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) who has greatest right over a woman and who over a man. He answered husband and mother. > **""Her husband. Her mother.""**"
"7646","Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a call to women to fear Allah and seek husbands' pleasure, for knowledge of the right would keep her standing through meals. > **""O assembly of women, fear Allah and seek your husbands' pleasure. If a woman knew her husband's right, she would remain standing while his lunch and dinner are present.""**"
"7647","Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said knowledge of a husband's right would keep a woman from sitting while his meals remain. > **""If a woman knew her husband's right, she would not sit while his lunch and dinner are present until he finishes.""**"
"7648","Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that Allah does not look at a wife ungrateful to a husband she needs. > **""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not look at a woman who is ungrateful to her husband though she cannot dispense with him.""**"
"7649","Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that he went to Syria, saw Christians prostrating to bishops, patriarchs, and monks and Jews to rabbis, scholars, and jurists, and was told it was the greeting of prophets. Thinking his Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) more deserving, he prostrated on return. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) corrected him, exposed their lie and alteration, and stressed a husband's right and obedience even on a camel's saddle as a condition of tasting faith. > **""What is this, O Muadh? They lied about their prophets as they altered their book. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a wife to prostrate to her husband due to his great right. No woman tastes the sweetness of faith until she fulfills her husband's right, even if he asks her while she is on a camel's saddle.""**"
"7650","Suhayb (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), after seeing Jews and Christians in Syria prostrate to scholars, rabbis, priests, jurists, and monks as prophetic greeting, prostrated to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on return and was corrected. > **""They lied about their prophets as they altered their book. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a wife to prostrate to her husband.""**"
"7651","Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) said the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) to Syria. On return Muadh asked, seeing People of the Book prostrate to bishops and patriarchs, whether they should not prostrate to him. He refused and stated the hypothetical command. > **""No. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a wife to prostrate to her husband.""**"
"7652","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stated the hypothetical command of a wife's prostration to her husband. > **""If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a wife to prostrate to her husband.""**"
"7653","Suraqah ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stated the hypothetical command of a wife's prostration to her husband. > **""If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a wife to prostrate to her husband.""**"
"7654","Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was among Muhajirun and Ansar when a camel came and prostrated to him. His companions said beasts and trees prostrate, so they were worthier to prostrate. He ordered worship of the Lord and honoring the brother, then stated the hypothetical command and a wife's duty even to move mountains. > **""Worship your Lord and honor your brother. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a wife to prostrate to her husband. If he ordered her to move from a yellow mountain to a black mountain, and from a mountain to a white mountain, she ought to do it.""**"
"7655","Ismah (may Allah be pleased with him) said an orphan Ansari boy's camel bolted and they could not seize it. They told the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who came to the enclosure. Seeing him, the camel advanced and prostrated. When they asked to prostrate as to kings, he refused and stated the hypothetical command for wives. > **""That is not in my nation. If I were to do so, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands.""**"
"7656","Ghaylan ibn Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) said they were with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on a journey when he stated the hypothetical command of a wife's prostration to her husband. > **""If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a wife to prostrate to her husband.""**"
"7657","Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed women sitting in the mosque, greeted them by hand signal, and warned against ingratitude to benefactors. When one sought refuge from ingratitude to Allah, he described long widowhood followed by husband, child, and comfort, then angry oaths of never seeing good. > **""Beware of ingratitude to benefactors. One of you remains long unmarried, long past youth, then Allah provides a husband, a child, and comfort. Then she angers and swears by Allah she never saw an hour of good from him. That is ingratitude to Allah's blessings, and that is ingratitude to benefactors.""**"
"7658","Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to women at the mosque side. Bold in speech to him, she asked why they were most of Hell's fuel. He named ingratitude when given, impatience when tried, complaint when withheld, and explained ingratitude of mothers of two or three who say they never saw good. > **""O assembly of women, you are most of Hell's fuel. When given, you are not grateful; when tried, you are not patient; and when withheld from, you complain. Beware of ingratitude to benefactors. What is ingratitude to benefactors? A woman lives with a man and bears him two or three children, then says: I never saw any good from you at all.""**"
"7659","Salma bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) said she pledged the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) among Ansari women, including not to deceive husbands. Returning, they asked what deception of husbands meant, and he explained gifts from his wealth to others. > **""That you not deceive your husbands. That you favor another with his wealth as gift.""**"
"7660","Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered a wife to answer her husband's call to bed even on a camel's saddle. > **""When a man calls his wife to his bed, let her respond, even if she is on a camel's saddle.""**"
"7661","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said a woman has two veils, her husband and her grave, and the grave conceals more. > **""A woman has two veils. What are they? Her husband and her grave. Which conceals more? The grave.""**"
"7662","Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) a list of men of Paradise — prophet, truthful, martyr, newborn, and one who visits his brother across town only for Allah — then of women: loving, fertile, who when angered, wronged, or her husband angered, places her hand in his and refuses sleep until pleased. > **""Shall I not tell you of your men in Paradise? The prophet in Paradise, the truthful in Paradise, the martyr in Paradise, the newborn in Paradise, and a man who visits his brother in another part of town only for Allah in Paradise. Shall I not tell you of your women in Paradise? Every loving, fertile one who, when angered, wronged, or her husband angered, says: Here is my hand in yours, I will not sleep until you are pleased.""**"
"7663","Kab ibn Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) listed men of Paradise — prophet, martyr, truthful, newborn, and visitor of his brother — then women: loving, fertile, who if she wrongs or is wronged places her forelock in her husband's hand and refuses sleep until pleased. > **""Shall I not tell you of your men among the people of Paradise? The prophet in Paradise, the martyr in Paradise, the truthful in Paradise, the newborn in Paradise, and a man who visits his brother in another part of town in Paradise. Shall I not tell you of your women among the people of Paradise? The loving, fertile one who, if she wrongs or is wronged, says: Here is my forelock in your hand, I will not taste sleep until you are pleased.""**"
"7664","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) a list of men of Paradise — prophet, truthful, martyr, Muslim newborn, and one who visits his brother across town only for Allah — then women: loving, fertile, who when angered says her hand is in her husband's and refuses sleep. > **""Shall I not tell you of your men among the people of Paradise? The prophet in Paradise, the truthful in Paradise, the martyr in Paradise, the Muslim newborn in Paradise, and a man on the side of town who visits his brother only for Allah in Paradise. Shall I not tell you of your women among the people of Paradise? The loving, fertile one who, when angered or angered, says: My hand is in yours, I will not sleep.""**"
"7665","Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that a wife may not admit one her husband dislikes, leave when he dislikes, obey another against him, roughen his heart, abandon his bed, nor strike him even if he wronged her, until she pleases him. If he accepts, Allah accepts her excuse; if not, she delivered her excuse. > **""It is not lawful for a wife to admit to her husband's house one he dislikes, nor leave when he dislikes, nor obey another in him, nor roughen his heart, nor abandon his bed, nor strike him, even if he is more unjust than her, until she pleases him. If he is pleased and accepts from her, well and good, Allah accepts her excuse and her face succeeds, with no sin upon her. If he refuses to be pleased with her, she has delivered her excuse.""**"
"7666","Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that a man left and ordered his wife not to leave home. Her father lived below, she above. When he sickened she asked permission to visit and was told to obey her husband. When he died she again was told to obey her husband. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent word of her father's forgiveness through her obedience. > **""Obey your husband. Obey your husband. Allah has forgiven her father through her obedience to her husband.""**"
"7667","Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) named three whose prayer is not accepted nor good deed raised: the intoxicated until sober, the wife with whom her husband is angry, and the runaway slave until he returns and places his hand in his masters' hands. > **""Three whose prayer is not accepted, nor good deed raised to Allah for them: the intoxicated until he sobers, the wife with whom her husband is angry, and the runaway slave until he returns and places his hand in his masters' hands.""**"
"7668","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) named two whose prayer does not pass their heads: the slave fleeing his masters until he returns, and the wife disobeying her husband until she returns. > **""Two whose prayer does not pass their heads: a slave fleeing his masters until he returns to them, and a wife disobeying her husband until she returns.""**"
"7669","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) warn that a woman leaving home against her husband's wish is cursed by every angel and everything she passes except jinn and men until she returns. > **""When a woman leaves her house while her husband dislikes it, every angel in heaven curses her, and everything she passes except jinn and men, until she returns.""**"
"7670","Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) expressed hatred for a woman who leaves home trailing her skirt while complaining of her husband. > **""I indeed detest a woman who leaves her house trailing her skirt, complaining of her husband.""**"
"7671","Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that woman is private, Satan gazes at her when she leaves, and she is nearest to Allah in her innermost home. > **""Woman is private, and when she leaves her house Satan gazes at her. She is never closer to Allah than in the depth of her house.""**"
"7672","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shibl رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Recite the Qur'an, and when you recite it, do not show arrogance through it, do not go to extremes in it, do not turn away from it, and do not earn a living through it.""** He ﷺ also said: > **""Women are the companions of the Fire.""** A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers, our sisters, and our daughters?"" The Prophet ﷺ then explained their ingratitude toward the rights of their husbands and their neglect of those rights."
"7673","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The Fire was created for the foolish, and they are women—except the one who obeys her husband.""**"
"7674","Tamīm al-Dārī رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The right of the husband over his wife is that she does not abandon his bed, that she fulfills his oath, that she obeys his command, that she does not leave except with his permission, and that she does not admit into his presence anyone he dislikes.""**"
"7675","Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām رضي الله عنه said: One day the Prophet ﷺ addressed the women, admonishing them and reminding them. He commanded them to fear Allah, to obey their husbands, and to give charity. He said: > **""Some of you will enter Paradise""** — and he joined his fingers together — **""but most of you are the fuel of Hell""** — and he separated his fingers. A woman said, ""Why, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: > **""Because you curse frequently, you are ungrateful to your husbands, and you delay doing good.""**"
"7676","Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr رضي الله عنها reported that she visited her sister ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها while al-Zubayr was away. The Prophet ﷺ entered and noticed the scent of perfume, so he said: > **""There is no harm upon a woman if she does not wear perfume while her husband is absent.""**"
"7677","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said, joining his fingers together: > **""What separates me from a woman with dust-stained cheeks—who is tender toward her child, obeys her Lord, and guards her chastity—is only like these two fingers.""**"
"7678","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: A woman said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward for a woman's devotion to her husband?"" He said: > **""Obedience to her husband and acknowledgment of his right.""**"
"7679","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed: > **""A woman may not give anything from her house except with her husband's permission.""**"
"7680","Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ رضي الله عنه said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""It is not permitted for a woman to dispose of anything from her wealth except with her husband's permission, once he possesses her in marriage.""**"
"7681","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: One night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told his wives a story, and one of the women said, ""O Messenger of Allah, it is as though this story is the story of Khurāfah."" He said: > **""Do you know who Khurāfah was? Khurāfah was a man of ʿUdhrah whom the jinn captured in the days of ignorance. He remained among them for a long time, then they returned him to mankind. He used to tell people of the wonders he had seen among them, so the people would say: the story of Khurāfah.""**"
"7682","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told her a story while sharing her quilt, and she said, ""May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah—had you not told me this story, I would have thought it was the story of Khurāfah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""And what is the story of Khurāfah, O ʿĀʾishah?""** She said, ""When something is untrue, it is called the story of Khurāfah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The truest of stories is the story of Khurāfah. Khurāfah was a man of Banū ʿUdhrah whom the jinn captured. He lived among them, and whenever they eavesdropped upon the heavens they would inform him, so he would tell the people, and they would find it exactly as he had said.""**"
"7683","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: I brought the Prophet ﷺ some ḥarīrah I had cooked for him, and I said to Sawdah—while the Prophet ﷺ was between me and her—""Eat."" She refused, so I said, ""Either you eat, or I will smear your face."" She refused, so I put my hand in the ḥarīrah and smeared her face. The Prophet ﷺ laughed and put his hand out for her, saying to her: > **""Smear her face.""** The Prophet ﷺ laughed for her. Then ʿUmar passed by, calling out, ""O ʿAbdullāh! O ʿAbdullāh!"" The Prophet ﷺ thought he would enter, so he said: > **""Get up and wash your faces.""** ʿĀʾishah said: I never ceased to hold ʿUmar in awe because of the awe the Messenger of Allah ﷺ showed him."
"7684","Ruzaynah, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reported that Sawdah al-Yamāniyyah came to visit ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها, while Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar رضي الله عنها was with her. Sawdah arrived adorned in fine condition, wearing a Yemeni cloak and head-cover, beautified with aloes and saffron. Ḥafṣah said to ʿĀʾishah, ""O Mother of the Believers, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is coming, and this woman will be glittering among us."" ʿĀʾishah said, ""Fear Allah, O Ḥafṣah."" Ḥafṣah said, ""I will spoil her adornment."" Sawdah was hard of hearing, so Ḥafṣah said to her, ""O Sawdah, the one-eyed one has come out!"" Sawdah was seized with terror and trembling, asking, ""Where shall I hide?"" They directed her to a palm-leaf shelter used for storage, full of dust and cobwebs, and she hid inside it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived, ʿĀʾishah and Ḥafṣah were laughing so hard they could barely speak. He asked three times: > **""Why are you laughing?""** They pointed toward the shelter. He went and found Sawdah trembling, and said: > **""What is wrong with you, O Sawdah?""** She said, ""O Messenger of Allah, has the one-eyed one come out?"" He said: > **""He has not come out, but he will surely come out.""** Then he brought her out, brushing the dust and cobwebs from her."
"7685","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ used to visit each of his wives every morning and greet them. One of them had honey, and whenever he entered upon her she would offer him some, so he would linger with her. ʿĀʾishah and Ḥafṣah رضي الله عنهما were troubled by this, and when he entered upon them they said, ""O Messenger of Allah, we detect upon you the scent of maghāfīr."" So he gave up that honey."
"7686","ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth رضي الله عنه said: Some Abyssinians were performing in Madinah, and ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها placed her shoulder upon the shoulder of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and watched them."
"7687","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: I boasted of my father's wealth in the days of ignorance—it amounted to a thousand thousand ounces—so the Prophet ﷺ said to me: > **""Be quiet, O ʿĀʾishah, for I am to you like Abū Zarʿ was to Umm Zarʿ.""** Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to narrate: eleven women gathered in the days of ignorance and pledged that each would truthfully describe her husband without lying. The first said her husband was like the night of Tihāmah—neither hot nor cold, neither frightening nor tiresome. The second praised her husband's sweet scent of zarnab, his soft touch like a rabbit, and that she prevailed over him while he prevailed over others. The third described her husband's lofty pillars, long sword-belt, abundant ashes of hospitality, and house near the gathering place. The fourth married Mālik, whose many camels seldom left their resting places, knowing slaughter awaited whenever they heard the lute. The fifth refused to describe her husband, fearing she would expose all his faults, hidden and open. The sixth said her husband was a leopard at home and a lion abroad, never questioned about his trusts. The seventh said her husband was like lean camel meat atop a rugged mountain—neither fat enough to carry away nor accessible to climb. The eighth said her husband devoured his food, gulped his drink, wrapped himself in sleep, and never lifted a hand to learn her sorrows. The ninth married a crooked stalk—divorce if she spoke, suspense if she stayed silent. The tenth said her husband was every disease combined—wounding, breaking, or both. Then Umm Zarʿ spoke: Abū Zarʿ filled her ears with jewelry and her arms with fat, honored her until she honored herself, moved her from a household of meager flocks to one of horses, camels, threshing, and winnowing. With him she spoke without reproach, slept into the morning, and drank her fill. His mother was generous with full vessels and a spacious house; his son slept in luxury and ate his fill; his daughter was obedient to both parents and envied by rivals; his maid kept the house clean without gossip. Then Abū Zarʿ divorced her and married another woman who gave him two lion-like sons, yet Umm Zarʿ said all of that woman's gifts could not fill one of Abū Zarʿ's vessels. The Prophet ﷺ concluded: > **""I am to you, O ʿĀʾishah, like Abū Zarʿ was to Umm Zarʿ—except that Abū Zarʿ divorced, while I will never divorce.""**"
"7688","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and said: > **""O ʿĀʾishah, I am to you like Abū Zarʿ was to Umm Zarʿ.""** The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that in a Yemeni town there were eleven women who gathered in a sitting and agreed to describe their husbands truthfully without lying: the first, then the second—ʿAmrah bint ʿAmr; the third—Ḥubbā bint Kaʿb; the fourth—Hudad, daughter of Abū Hirawah; the fifth—Kabshah; the sixth—Hind; the seventh—Ḥubbā bint ʿAlqamah; the eighth—Asmāʾ bint ʿAbd; the ninth—whose name was not given; the tenth—Kabshah bint al-Arqam; and Umm Zarʿ, daughter of Ukayḥil ibn Sāʿidah, who said, ""Abū Zarʿ—oh, what of Abū Zarʿ!""—and he narrated the full account."
"7689","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ said that eleven women gathered in the days of ignorance and pledged to speak truthfully about their husbands, concealing nothing. The first said her husband was like lean camel meat atop a mountain peak—neither easy to climb nor fat enough to carry away. The second refused to expose her husband's faults, hidden and open. The third said her husband was a crooked stalk—divorce if she spoke, suspense if she stayed silent. The fourth said her husband devoured his food, gulped his drink, wrapped himself in sleep, and never reached out a hand to learn her sorrows. The fifth said her husband was impotent and dull—every disease in one—wounding her, breaking her, or both. The sixth said her husband was like the night of Tihāmah—neither hot nor cold, and without fear. The seventh said her husband was a leopard indoors and a lion outdoors, never questioned about his trusts. The eighth said her husband's touch was like a rabbit and his scent like zarnab, and that she prevailed over him while he prevailed over others. The ninth said her husband had lofty pillars, a long sword-belt, abundant ashes, and a house near the gathering place. The tenth said her husband Mālik—oh, what of Mālik—owned camels that seldom went to pasture and mostly stayed resting, knowing slaughter awaited at the sound of the lute. The eleventh, Umm Zarʿ, said: Abū Zarʿ—oh, what of Abū Zarʿ—he filled her ears with jewelry and her arms with fat, honored her until she honored herself, moved her from a household of meager flocks to one of horses, camels, threshing, and winnowing. With him she spoke without reproach, slept into the morning, and drank her fill. His mother was generous with full vessels and a spacious house; his son was pampered in sleep and food; his daughter was obedient and envied; his maid was tidy and discreet. Then the Prophet ﷺ said to ʿĀʾishah: > **""I am to you like Abū Zarʿ was to Umm Zarʿ.""**"
"7690","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ along with his Companions when a scantily clad woman approached. A man from the company stood, threw a garment over her, and drew her to himself. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed color. One of his Companions said, ""I suppose she is his wife."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""I do not think she is other than jealous. Allah has decreed jealousy upon women and striving upon men—so whoever among them is patient will have the reward of a martyr.""**"
"7691","Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ performed pilgrimage with his wives. Along the way a driver urged the camels on swiftly, so the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Gently—your driving of the glass vessels.""** —meaning the women. As they traveled, the camel of Ṣafiyyah رضي الله عنها knelt, though hers was among the finest mounts, and she wept. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and wiped her tears with his hand while forbidding her to weep, but she wept more, so he rebuked her and ordered the people to halt—though he had not intended to halt. That day belonged to her. When the tents were pitched and he entered his tent, she feared resentment lingered in him, so she went to ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها and said, ""You know I would never sell my day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for anything—but I give my day to you, if you will reconcile the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with me."" ʿĀʾishah agreed. She perfumed her veil with saffron, sprinkled it with water to release its fragrance, dressed herself, and went to the Prophet ﷺ, lifting the edge of the tent. He said: > **""What is wrong with you, O ʿĀʾishah? This is not your day.""** She said, ""That is the bounty of Allah—He gives it to whom He wills."" He stayed with her household. When it was time to depart, he said to Zaynab bint Jaḥsh رضي الله عنها: > **""Lend your sister Ṣafiyyah a camel.""** She was the one with the most mounts. She said, ""Should I lend to your Jewess?"" The Prophet ﷺ grew angry and boycotted her for the rest of Dhū al-Ḥijjah, Muḥarram, Ṣafar, and part of Rabīʿ al-Awwal, until she packed away her bedding, thinking he had no need of her—then he returned to her."
"7692","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: Ṣafiyyah sent the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some food she had prepared for him while he was with me. When I saw the servant girl, trembling seized me until my joints shook, and I struck the bowl and threw it. I looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and recognized anger in his face, so I said, ""I seek refuge with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lest he curse me today."""
"7693","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: Umm Salamah was with us when the Prophet ﷺ came in the early night. I mentioned something he had made with his hand, and Umm Salamah did not notice it, so I gestured to him until he understood. Umm Salamah said, ""Is this how it is now—can none of us be with you except in private?"" and she reviled ʿĀʾishah. The Prophet ﷺ kept forbidding her, but she refused, so the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Answer her back.""** So ʿĀʾishah reviled her until she overcame her. Then Umm Salamah went to ʿAlī and Fāṭimah رضي الله عنهما and complained that ʿĀʾishah had reviled her and spoken against them. ʿAlī sent Fāṭimah to the Prophet ﷺ to complain, but he said to her: > **""She is the beloved of your father, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah.""** So she returned to ʿAlī and told him what the Prophet ﷺ had said."
"7694","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: My provisions were light, carried on a swift camel, while Ṣafiyyah's provisions were heavy, carried on a slow, weak camel that delayed the caravan. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Transfer ʿĀʾishah's provisions onto Ṣafiyyah's camel, and transfer Ṣafiyyah's provisions onto ʿĀʾishah's camel, so the caravan may proceed.""** When I saw that, I said, ""O servants of Allah, this Jewess has overcome us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""O Umm ʿAbdillāh, your provisions were light and Ṣafiyyah's provisions were heavy, delaying the caravan, so we transferred her provisions onto your camel and your provisions onto hers.""** I said, ""Do you not claim that you are the Messenger of Allah? Then why do you not act justly?"" Abū Bakr رضي الله عنه heard me—he was sharp-tempered—and came toward me and struck my face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Gently, O Abā Bakr.""** Abū Bakr said, ""O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear what she said?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The jealous one cannot distinguish the bottom of the valley from its top.""**"
"7695","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey with us when Ṣafiyyah's camel fell ill, while Zaynab had a spare mount. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: > **""Ṣafiyyah's camel has fallen ill—if only you would give her one of your camels.""** She said, ""Should I give to this Jewess?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ grew angry and boycotted her for the rest of Dhū al-Ḥijjah, Muḥarram, Ṣafar, and some days of Rabīʿ al-Awwal, until she packed away her bedding and her furnishings, thinking he had no need of her. Then one midday, as she sat, she saw his shadow approaching, so she set her bedding and furnishings back in place."
"7696","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""When a man marries a virgin, he stays with her for three days.""**"
"7697","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The virgin has seven days, and the previously married woman has three.""**"
"7698","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended a journey, he would cast lots among his wives—and the lot fell to ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها in the campaign of Banū al-Muṣṭaliq."
"7699","Sawdah bint Zamʿah رضي الله عنها gave her allotted day to ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها."
"7700","Abū Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The maternal aunt is a mother.""**"
"7701","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr رضي الله عنهما reported that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, this son of mine—my womb was a vessel for him, my lap a shelter for him, and my breast a drink for him—yet his father claims he will take him from me."" He said: > **""You have more right to him so long as you do not remarry.""**"
"7702","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah, ʿAlī brought out the daughter of Ḥamzah رضي الله عنهم. ʿAlī, Jaʿfar, and Zayd disputed over her before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿAlī said, ""My uncle's daughter, and I brought her out."" Jaʿfar said, ""My uncle's daughter, and her maternal aunt is with me."" Zayd said, ""My brother's daughter""—for Zayd had been made the brother of Ḥamzah by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Zayd: > **""You are my freedman and hers.""** And he said to ʿAlī: > **""You are my brother and my companion.""** And he said to Jaʿfar: > **""You resemble me in appearance and character—and she goes to her maternal aunt.""**"
"7703","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Help comes from Allah according to the burden of need, and patience comes from Allah according to the measure of affliction.""**"
"7704","ʿAmr ibn Umayyah رضي الله عنه reported that ʿUmar met him in the market while he was bargaining for a cloak, and asked, ""What is this, O ʿAmr?"" He said, ""A cloak I bought to give in charity."" Later ʿUmar asked him what he had done with the cloak, and he said he had given it in charity to Sukhaylah bint ʿUbaydah. ʿUmar questioned him, so ʿAmr said he had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whatever you give them of anything, it is charity for you.""** ʿUmar refused to part from him until they came to ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها, the Mother of the Believers. ʿAmr adjured her by Allah whether she had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whatever you give them, it is charity for you?""** She said, ""O Allah, yes! O Allah, yes!"" So ʿUmar said, ""Where was I from this? Bargaining in the markets distracted me."""
"7705","ʿAmr ibn Umayyah رضي الله عنه said: ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān—or ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf—passed by a cloak and deemed it costly. Then he passed it by ʿAmr ibn Umayyah, who bought it and clothed his wife Sukhaylah bint ʿUbaydah with it. Later he was asked what became of the cloak, and he said he had given it in charity to Sukhaylah bint ʿUbaydah. It was said to him: > **""Everything you do for your family is charity.""** ʿAmr said he had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that, and when it was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: > **""ʿAmr has spoken the truth. Everything you do for your family is charity upon them.""**"
"7706","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The first thing placed in the servant's scale is his spending upon his family.""**"
"7707","Al-ʿIrbāḍ ibn Sāriyah رضي الله عنه said that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""When a man gives his wife water to drink, he is rewarded.""** So he went to her, gave her water to drink, and told her what he had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."
"7708","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""It suffices a man as sin that he neglects those he sustains.""**"
"7709","Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah رضي الله عنه said: The Prophet ﷺ passed by me, and the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ noticed vigor and energy in me, so they said, ""O Messenger of Allah, if only this were in the path of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""If he went out striving for his small children, then he is in the path of Allah. If he went out striving for his two aged parents, then he is in the path of Allah. If he went out striving for himself to keep himself chaste, then he is in the path of Allah. But if he went out striving for show and boasting, then he is in the path of Satan.""**"
"7710","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The one who strives for his parents to suffice them or free them of need from people is in the path of Allah. The one who strives for himself to enrich himself or free himself of need from people is in the path of Allah. And the one who strives for rivalry is in the path of Satan.""**"
"7711","ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd Abū ʿAmr, under whom was Fāṭimah bint Qays, divorced her. She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: > **""She has no maintenance.""**"
"7712","ʿAmr and Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنهما said that the woman divorced three times is entitled to lodging and maintenance."
"7713","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما was asked about the pregnant woman whose husband has died, and he said: we used to spend upon her."
"7714","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that a man divorced his wife, and she came to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: > **""You have neither maintenance nor lodging.""**"
"7715","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that a man arrived from a journey, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: > **""Did you stay with so-and-so woman and lock her door upon yourself?""** He said, ""Yes."" The Prophet ﷺ disapproved of that."
"7716","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No man may enter upon a woman except with a maḥram of hers present.""**"
"7717","Abū Umāmah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Beware of being alone with women. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, no man is alone with a woman but that Satan enters between them—and for a man to crowd against a pig smeared with mud and filth is better for him than for his shoulder to press against the shoulder of a woman who is not lawful to him.""**"
"7718","Maʿqil ibn Yasār رضي الله عنه said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""For an iron needle to be thrust into the head of one of you is better for him than to touch a woman who is not lawful to him.""**"
"7719","Anas رضي الله عنه said: On the morning after I first experienced a wet dream, I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said: > **""Do not enter upon women.""** No day weighed upon me more heavily than that one."
"7720","Saʿīd ibn Zayd رضي الله عنه said that after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, Fāṭimah would uncover her head when a young boy entered, but cover it when a grown man entered."
"7721","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Three have been forbidden Paradise by Allah: the habitual wine-drinker, the disobedient to parents, and the cuckold who approves filth in his household.""**"
"7722","ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Three will never enter Paradise: the cuckold, the masculine woman, and the habitual wine-drinker.""** They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, as for the habitual wine-drinker, we know him—but what is the cuckold?"" He said: > **""The one who does not care who enters upon his household.""** They said, ""And what is the masculine woman?"" He said: > **""The one who imitates men.""**"
"7723","Mālik ibn Uḥaymir رضي الله عنه said that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Allah will accept neither compensation nor recompense on the Day of Resurrection from the procurers.""** They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, and who are the procurers?"" He said: > **""The one who brings men into his household.""**"
"7724","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah is jealous for His believing servant—so let a man be jealous for himself.""**"
"7725","Abū Saʿīd رضي الله عنه said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Jealousy is from faith, and indifference is from hypocrisy.""** He said, ""I asked: what is indifference?"" He said: > **""The one who is not jealous.""**"
"7726","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""I am jealous, and Allah is more jealous than I—and Allah loves the jealous among His servants.""**"
"7727","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""ʿUmar is jealous, and I am more jealous than he, and Allah is more jealous than us.""**"
"7728","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, do you not feel jealousy?"" He said: > **""By Allah, I am jealous, and Allah is more jealous than I—and from His jealousy He forbade immoralities.""**"
"7729","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: When the verse ""Those who accuse chaste women and do not bring four witnesses"" was revealed, Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah said, ""If I were to see a man with my wife, should I wait until I bring four witnesses?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: > **""Yes.""** He said, ""No—by the One who sent you with the truth, if I saw him I would strike him down with the sword."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Look, O company of the Anṣār, at what your chief says. Saʿd is jealous, and I am more jealous than he, and Allah is more jealous than I.""**"
"7730","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: When ""Those who accuse chaste women and do not bring four witnesses—flog them eighty lashes and never accept their testimony"" was revealed, Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, the chief of the Anṣār, said, ""Was it revealed like this, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""O company of the Anṣār, do you not hear what your chief says?""** They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, do not blame him, for he is a jealous man. By Allah, he never married any woman except a virgin, nor ever divorced a wife of his but that none of us dared to marry her after him, from the severity of his jealousy."" Saʿd said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I know it is true and from Allah, but I am amazed—if I found a vile woman with a man upon her, I would have no right to disturb or move him until I bring four witnesses. By Allah, I would not bring them until he had fulfilled his need."""
"7731","ʿAmr ibn Shuraḥbīl, narrating from his father from his grandfather, said: Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, if I find a man upon my wife's belly, shall I strike him with my sword? What proof is clearer than the sword?"" Then he retracted his statement and said, ""The Book of Allah and the witnesses."" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""O company of the Anṣār, this chief of yours—jealousy has provoked him until he opposed the Book of Allah.""** A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, Saʿd is jealous—he never divorced a woman but that none of us could marry her after him, because of his jealousy."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Saʿd is jealous, and I am more jealous than he, and Allah is more jealous than I.""** A man said, ""Over what is Allah jealous?"" He said: > **""Over a fighter in the path of Allah who is betrayed with respect to his household.""**"
"7732","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه said: There was much talk about Māriyah, the mother of Ibrāhīm, concerning a Coptic cousin of hers who visited her and frequented her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: > **""Take this sword and go—if you find him with her, kill him.""** I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, when you send me on your command, shall I be like the heated rail—nothing turning me aside until I carry out what you commanded—or shall the witness see what the absent one does not see?"" He said: > **""Rather, the witness sees what the absent one does not see.""** So I set out girded with the sword and found him with her. I drew the sword, and when he saw me advancing toward him, he knew I meant him—so he went to a palm tree, climbed it, then threw himself down upon his back and spread his legs, revealing that he was a castrated eunuch with neither little nor much. I sheathed the sword and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, and he said: > **""Praise be to Allah, who averts evil from us, the Household.""**"
"7733","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه said: When Ibrāhīm, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was born to Māriyah, something entered the heart of the Prophet ﷺ about him—until Jibrīl عليه السلام came to him and said: > **""Peace upon you, father of Ibrāhīm.""**"
"7734","ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī رضي الله عنه said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There are two kinds of jealousy—one Allah loves and one Allah hates. Jealousy with grounds for suspicion, Allah loves; jealousy without grounds for suspicion, Allah hates. And there are two kinds of pride—one Allah loves and one Allah hates. Pride when a man gives charity, Allah loves; pride in arrogance, Allah hates.""** And he said: > **""Three have their supplication answered: the traveler, the parent, and the oppressed.""**"
"7735","Anas ibn Mālik رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ would not come to his family by night—he would enter in the morning or in the evening."
"7736","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted at al-ʿAqīq and forbade coming to women by night unannounced. Two men disobeyed him, and each of them saw what he disliked."
"7737","Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqās رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to come to his family by night after the ʿIshāʾ prayer."
"7738","ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah رضي الله عنه returned from a journey in haste and found a lamp in his house, with something beside his wife. He seized his sword, but she said, ""Keep away from me—so-and-so's wife is combing my hair."" He went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and the Prophet forbade a man to come to his family by night unannounced."
"7739","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Do not come to women by night""** —meaning that when one of you returns from a journey, he should not come to his family except by day. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then returned from a journey, but two men hastened ahead despite the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and came to their families—and each of them found a man with his wife."
"7740","Naḍlah ibn Ṭarīf reported that a man of theirs called al-Aʿshā—whose name was ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Aʿwar—had a wife called Muʿādhah. He went out in Rajab to fetch provisions for his family from Hajar, and after him his wife fled in rebellion against him, seeking refuge with a man of theirs called Muṭarrif ibn Buhṣul. When the husband returned and did not find her in his house, he was told she had rebelled against him and sought refuge with Muṭarrif. He came to him and said, ""O cousin, my wife Muʿādhah is with you—hand her over to me."" He said, ""She is not with me—and even if she were with me, I would not hand her over to you."" Muṭarrif was mightier than he, so the husband went to the Prophet ﷺ, sought refuge with him, and recited verses complaining of her sharp tongue and flight: ""O master of men and judge of the Arabs—to you I complain of a considerable sharpness, like the dusky wolf in the shade of the thicket. I went out seeking food for her in Rajab, but she left me behind in strife and fled. She broke the covenant and turned her back, casting me among tangled thickets—and they are the worst conquerors for the conqueror."" The Prophet ﷺ repeated at that: > **""And they are the worst conquerors for the conqueror.""** He complained to him of his wife and what she had done, and that she was with Muṭarrif ibn Buhṣul. So the Prophet ﷺ wrote for him to Muṭarrif: > **""To Muṭarrif: the wife of this man, Muʿādhah—hand her over to him.""** The letter of the Prophet ﷺ reached Muṭarrif and was read to him, so he said to her, ""O Muʿādhah, this is the letter of the Prophet ﷺ concerning you, and I shall hand you over to him."" She said, ""Take for me his covenant, pledge, and the protection of the Prophet ﷺ that he will not punish me for what I did."" So he took that pledge for her from him, and Muṭarrif handed her over to him. Then the husband recited: ""By your life, my love for Muʿādhah is not such that slanderers or the length of time can change—nor the evil she brought when the corrupt men lured her away in my absence."""
"7741","Al-Aʿshā al-Māzinī said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and recited to him: ""O king of men and judge of the Arabs—I have met a considerable sharpness. I went out early seeking food for her in Rajab, but she left me behind in strife and fled. She broke the covenant and turned her back—and they are the worst conquerors for the conqueror."" The Prophet ﷺ kept repeating at that: > **""And they are the worst conquerors for the conqueror.""**"
"7742","Buraydah رضي الله عنه said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""He is not from us who swears by trust, and whoever corrupts a wife against her husband or a slave against his master is not from us.""**"
"7743","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""He is not from us who corrupts a woman against her husband, and he is not from us who corrupts a slave against his master.""**"
"7744","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever wears silk and drinks from silver is not from us—and whoever corrupts a woman against her husband or a slave against his masters is not from us.""**"
"7745","ʿAlī رضي الله عنه reported that the wife of al-Walīd ibn ʿUqbah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, al-Walīd beats her""—complaining of him. He said: > **""Tell him: he has granted me protection.""** ʿAlī said: she stayed away only a short while, then returned and said, ""He has only beaten me more."" So he took a fringe of his garment and handed it to her, saying: > **""Tell him: the Messenger of Allah has granted me protection.""** She stayed away only a short while, then returned and said, ""He has only beaten me more."" So he raised his hands and said: > **""O Allah, deal with al-Walīd—he has sinned against me.""** —twice."
"7746","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that some men complained of their wives to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he permitted them to strike them. That night many women gathered, complaining. She said: what Muslim women have met! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Strike them—but the best of you will not strike.""**"
"7747","On the authority of Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I went into the house of Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he had locked the door upon Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) — and she was the mother of Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) — while he was striking her. So I called out from behind the door: > **""What do you want with this old woman that you keep striking her?""** Then she called out to me from behind the door and said to me: > **""You say 'the old woman'? May Allah make your knees feeble.""**"
